/* 7-letter-cap stories: 300 parodies, generated by tools/build-word-readers.mjs from library/word-stories.json. Do not edit. */
window.READERS.push(
  { id: "w7-006-the-crown-in-the-well", title: "The crown in the well", pay: 214200, lib: 7, text: "King Kit dropped his crown in a well. Finn, a monkey in a frog suit, said a kiss would bring it back. Kit peered down and saw the crown caught on a nail. He lent Finn his long tail as a rope. Finn fetched it, but the wet suit stuck to his fur. Kit paid him bananas and a dry towel. Finn quit the frog act and opened a tool shop." },
  { id: "w7-012-the-dragon-needs-a-shelf", title: "The dragon needs a shelf", pay: 217600, lib: 7, text: "Sir Nim rode to a cave to face a dragon. Drake was a large monkey with a smoke pot and wings of cloth. His heap of bananas kept falling on the pot, so the cave smelled burnt. Nim put down his lance and built a shelf. Drake stacked the fruit on it and took off the wings. Nim earned a medal for fire safety, though he asked for a chair instead." },
  { id: "w7-001-the-pea-with-a-receipt", title: "The pea with a receipt", pay: 217600, lib: 7, text: "Queen Ada hid a pea beneath the guest bed. Pip, a small monkey, felt no lump at all. His tail did find a receipt that said the bed cost ten bananas. He took the receipt to Ada and asked why a fine bed had loose springs. Ada tried it herself. One spring poked her fur. She hired Pip to mend the bed and served the pea in soup." },
  { id: "w7-002-a-slipper-for-the-wrong-foot", title: "A slipper for the wrong foot", pay: 221000, lib: 7, text: "Moss left one glass shoe at the ball. Prince Jem toured the woods with it, sure he would find his bride. Each monkey tried a foot. Moss tried his tail. The shoe fit that best, since he had worn it as a tail bell all night. Jem felt a bit silly. They hung the shoe over the gate and rang it when fresh bananas came to the hall." },
  { id: "w7-034-the-ginger-hut-lease", title: "The ginger hut lease", pay: 221000, lib: 7, text: "Hal found a hut made of cake and bit the wall. Bess came out with a rent bill. The monkey said he thought it was a free sample. Bess showed him the plain door and asked him to mend the hole before rain came. Hal baked a brick of oats and bananas. It fit snugly. Bess hung a Sample sign on a tray outside, and Hal became her first regular guest." },
  { id: "w7-041-the-royal-pumpkin-cart", title: "The royal pumpkin cart", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Fay turned a pumpkin into a cart for Cindy. At twelve it would turn back. Cindy, a monkey who hated waste, drove to the ball with bowls and a spoon. When the clock struck, she parked beside the kitchen. The wheels became seeds and the cart became a large pumpkin. She made soup for the late guests and packed bananas for the walk home. Fay admired the empty peel at dawn." },
  { id: "w7-063-the-tennis-moon-shot", title: "The tennis moon shot", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Amy hit a tennis ball into the clouds. Dot praised her power, then asked how to win a point without a ball. The monkey tried a softer serve. It rolled under the net and hit a crate of bananas. Dot used a lid as a low target. Amy hit it ten times, then served over the net at last. The lost ball fell on the court at dusk and scored nothing at all." },
  { id: "w7-109-the-distant-planet-mud", title: "The distant planet mud", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Sky found a strange brown sea on a new planet. Cam said the monkey must bring a sample home. Sky dipped his tail in and got stuck. Cam pulled him free with a rope. The sea was deep mud, much like the patch behind their hut. They marked it on the map and took a jar anyway. Back home they grew bananas in it, which earned the planet a useful name, Garden." },
  { id: "w7-004-the-wolf-stamp", title: "The wolf stamp", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Bo cried that a wolf had come. No wolf came, but all the monkeys left their work. Wren gave him a red stamp to use for real danger. Bo stamped his own fur just to test it. The mark would not wash off. When a wolf did pass, Bo held up his red tail. The troop shut the gate, then paid him bananas to guard it with a plain bell." },
  { id: "w7-023-a-troll-with-a-ticket", title: "A troll with a ticket", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Tom sat under the bridge and charged a riddle as toll. June, a monkey bus driver, had twenty guests who all gave the same wrong guess. Tom would not let them pass. June handed him a ticket and a bunch of bananas. He rode across with them to see where the bus went. At the far bank he found a riddle club and stayed there, leaving the bridge free for traffic." },
  { id: "w7-039-the-sand-castle-king", title: "The sand castle king", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Kip ruled a sand castle and charged monkeys bananas to enter. Uma warned him that the tide would soon reach the gate. Kip ordered a taller wall. Uma dug a ditch instead and led the water around the yard. The castle still fell at dusk, but the guests had dry fur. Kip gave them their fruit back. Next day he made a sand park with free gates and a tide sign." },
  { id: "w7-072-the-alarm-duck", title: "The alarm duck", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Hett heard a loud quack and flew to the pond. Dan, a monkey in a duck suit, was testing the village alarm. Hett saved him from a puddle he meant to sit in. Dan made a sign that said Test Day. Hett helped hang it beside the bell and waited for a real call. When a cart tipped, they both went to lift it. The driver gave them bananas and a quiet thank you." },
  { id: "w7-176-the-remote-office-branch", title: "The remote office branch", pay: 224400, lib: 7, text: "Amber sent Arbor a desk for remote work. The monkey lived in a tree, where the flat desk could not fit between the limbs. Arbor hung its drawers from ropes and used one as a lap tray. Amber saw him work well on a video call. She asked where the desk top had gone. Arbor aimed the camera below. It was a roof over the mail box, keeping every letter dry." },
  { id: "w7-127-the-jewel-ice-cube", title: "The jewel ice cube", pay: 227800, lib: 7, text: "Hana lost a blue gem at the feast. Dune checked every monkey pocket and found only crumbs. His own drink had a blue ice cube. He let it melt in a dish, and the gem fell out. Hana had dropped it while filling the ice tray. Dune gave it back and drank plain water. Hana served bananas in dry bowls so no one had to wait for dessert to thaw." },
  { id: "w7-030-the-crow-pebble-tax", title: "The crow pebble tax", pay: 227800, lib: 7, text: "Cam wore black wings and dropped stones in a jug to raise its water. Willa watched the monkey work for an hour. Each stone cost him a banana at the stone stall. She tipped the jug into a shallow bowl. Cam drank, then took the stones back and got his bananas back. He kept one smooth stone as a weight so his new bowl would not blow away in the wind." },
  { id: "w7-107-the-comet-pet-race", title: "The comet pet race", pay: 227800, lib: 7, text: "Kit kept Coco as a pet comet in a glass bowl. Coco was a monkey with a silver cape who ran in circles so fast the bowl shook. Kit asked him to stop for bananas. Coco stopped at once, and the bowl fell quiet. They moved the game outside to a wide field. Kit drew a slow orbit round the picnic cloth. Coco could race each lap and still sit down for a snack." },
  { id: "w7-051-the-pancake-ceiling", title: "The pancake ceiling", pay: 227800, lib: 7, text: "Chip flipped his pancake so high it stuck to the ceiling. Judge Jo waited with her fork. The monkey chef climbed a shelf, but his tail knocked flour over the stove. Jo handed him a mop. Chip swept the cake down onto a clean tray and served it with bananas. Jo gave him a prize for floor care. He hung it at eye level and kept each new flip below it." },
  { id: "w7-102-the-alien-doorbell", title: "The alien doorbell", pay: 227800, lib: 7, text: "Sia heard a ring outside her ship. Avo stood there with a plate of bananas and a long green hat. The monkey scout thought the hat was an alien weapon. Avo took it off and showed more fruit inside. He had come to trade hats for spoons. Sia gave him one spoon and took the hat. They rang the bell twice for friends, then sat on the ramp and ate." },
  { id: "w7-029-the-lion-net-review", title: "The lion net review", pay: 227800, lib: 7, text: "Leo wore a lion mane and laughed at tiny Min. Then his mane caught in a net while he chased bananas. Min was a small monkey with neat claws. She cut one knot and let him crawl out. Leo offered her a place on his royal staff. Min asked for a stool at the fruit stall instead. He built it that day, and she could reach the ripe bunches without his help." },
  { id: "w7-037-the-spindle-cap", title: "The spindle cap", pay: 227800, lib: 7, text: "Rose found a spindle in the attic, despite a royal ban. The monkey touched its point and got a small prick. Aunt Eve heard her yelp and brought a bandage. No one fell asleep. Rose asked why the king had banned all sewing. Eve showed her a cap that kept the sharp tip covered. They made caps for every spindle and used the saved cloth to wrap bananas for the winter fair." },
  { id: "w7-008-the-mirror-takes-a-day-off", title: "The mirror takes a day off", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Queen Bea asked her mirror who had the best fur. The mirror gave no reply. Dot, the monkey who cleaned it, found a leaf stuck over its mouth. Bea pulled the leaf away. The mirror asked who had the best manners. Bea brought Dot a chair and some bananas while she worked. The mirror praised the clean glass. Bea liked that answer enough to stop asking about her own fur." },
  { id: "w7-025-the-moon-cheese-trial", title: "The moon cheese trial", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Otto saw the moon in a pond and thought it was cheese. He told the other monkeys to drain the pond. Sage Tess put a bowl of water beside it. The moon shone in that too. Otto tried a spoon and got only water on his fur. Tess gave him cheese on a leaf with ripe bananas. He ate that and left the moon in the pond so fish could have a lamp." },
  { id: "w7-141-the-silver-trail-snail", title: "The silver trail snail", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Drake saw a silver trail near the locked fruit shed. The monkey thought a thief had dragged a chain there. Greta lent him a lens, and he traced the trail to a snail. It had crossed a wet leaf in the moon glow. Drake opened the shed with Greta and found the bananas safe. He moved the snail to a damp patch beside the fence. Greta gave him the lens to check small facts first." },
  { id: "w7-011-a-boot-full-of-wishes", title: "A boot full of wishes", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Fairy Rue gave Sol three wishes. Sol wished for more bananas, then for a boot to hold them all. The boot grew so large that it blocked his hut. His monkey tail stuck beneath the heel. Rue waited for his last wish. Sol asked for the boot to have wheels. He rolled it to the square and made a fruit cart. Rue bought the first bunch and got a free ride." },
  { id: "w7-007-the-three-small-inns", title: "The three small inns", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Ash built an inn of straw. Elm used sticks. Oak used brick. Their monkey guests ate bananas in all three. A great wind blew down the first two inns, and all the guests ran to Oak. His door was too small for the crowd. Ash wove a broad mat roof and Elm built a long bench in the yard. Oak sold his bricks to buy tea for the new open inn." },
  { id: "w7-045-the-queen-of-crumbs", title: "The queen of crumbs", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Qia claimed every crumb on the bakery floor as royal land. Bo swept the crumbs up before she could build her palace. The monkey queen sat on his broom and refused to move. Bo gave her a tray where crumbs could stay dry. Qia made a tiny castle on it and charged ants a leaf to enter. Bo served bananas beside her tray, and the ants left his good bread alone." },
  { id: "w7-049-the-marble-egg-mother", title: "The marble egg mother", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Mae found a marble egg and sat on it for days. Cora, a young monkey, brought her bananas while she waited for it to hatch. At last Cora saw a small hole through the stone. It was a bead from the royal curtain. Mae gave it back and got a soft cushion as thanks. She sat on that instead. Cora used the cushion box as a nest for toy birds that hatched on time." },
  { id: "w7-110-the-moon-flag-laundry", title: "The moon flag laundry", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Cal planted his flag on the moon, but Cia noticed it was a wet towel. The monkey captain had grabbed it from the wash rack. Cal wanted to leave it as a grand symbol. Cia needed it to dry her fur. They took a photo, folded the towel, and drew a flag on a flat stone. At home they ate bananas beneath the photo, while the real towel dried on its proper line." },
  { id: "w7-113-the-spy-door-password", title: "The spy door password", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Elm reached the secret door but forgot the code. Glen offered a hint, saying it was a yellow fruit. The monkey tried lemon, then mango, then pear. His tail brushed a crate of bananas beside the wall. Glen pointed at it. Elm spoke the right word and entered. Inside, he changed the code to Tail so he would always have a hint with him. Glen moved the fruit crate into the kitchen." },
  { id: "w7-065-the-jump-pole-lunch", title: "The jump pole lunch", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Jem used a tall pole to leap over a bar. Kim saw him stop halfway and pick bananas from a branch. The monkey said his grip needed a snack. Kim moved the bar to an open field. Jem jumped cleanly, then missed the branch where he had planned to land. Kim placed a soft mat there. Jem won the event and ate his fruit on the ground, with the pole flat beside him." },
  { id: "w7-138-the-spy-pigeon-basket", title: "The spy pigeon basket", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Dove sent a message by pigeon, but the bird landed at the fruit stall. Dovea found it pecking bananas beside the monkey agent. Dove saw he had used a page covered in fruit stains. He wrote a clean copy and tucked it into a dry tube. Dovea sent the bird again. It reached the right hut before dusk. Dove washed his desk and ate the ripe fruit far from his paper stack." },
  { id: "w7-010-the-goose-on-a-break", title: "The goose on a break", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "May kept a goose that laid gold eggs. Gil was a monkey in a feather cape, and the eggs were brass balls from his shed. May asked for ten more each day. Gil put down his cape and showed her his sore hands. May helped polish the old balls. They sold them as door bells and split the bananas they earned. The goose nest became a soft chair for both to rest." },
  { id: "w7-026-the-acorn-budget", title: "The acorn budget", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Amy stored acorns for winter. Gil played songs and stored none. The monkeys met when snow sealed the nut shed. Amy could not reach its latch through the drift. Gil tapped a tune on the roof until the loose snow slid off. Amy opened the shed and shared nuts and bananas. Gil played while she counted the sacks. In spring he built a drum with a small food bin inside it." },
  { id: "w7-069-the-gold-medal-weight", title: "The gold medal weight", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Lou trained to lift the largest weight in the hall. He won a gold medal so heavy it pulled his neck down. The monkey asked Cole to help him wear it. Cole put it on a stand, but the stand sank into the soft floor. Lou used the medal as a door wedge and hung a small leaf on his chest. He could carry his bananas again, which felt like a better prize." },
  { id: "w7-003-the-bean-pole-toll", title: "The bean pole toll", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Nell grew a bean stalk so tall that clouds caught in its leaves. Giant Gus charged each monkey three bananas to climb it. Nell saw that he used the toll to buy boots that crushed her beans. She set a small stall at the root and sold bean soup. Gus climbed down for lunch. His boots sank in the mud, so he stayed to help pick beans in bare feet." },
  { id: "w7-145-the-attic-footstep-drum", title: "The attic footstep drum", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Hark heard heavy steps in the attic each night. He climbed up with a lamp, his monkey tail stiff with fear. Harp sat there beating a drum with her feet while she ate bananas. She played after dark because the attic was cool. Hark moved a chair and rug up to soften the sound. Harp played him a quiet tune. The house stayed calm. Hark slept till dawn with his lamp off." },
  { id: "w7-153-the-inbox-nest", title: "The inbox nest", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Corin printed every unread note and built a nest beneath his desk. Brin wanted the monkey to answer them all. Corin sorted the pages by date and found most asked about a feast held last year. He filed those in a box and handled the three new queries. Brin gave him bananas for lunch. Corin used the empty nest as a foot rest, and Brin stopped sending each note to every desk." },
  { id: "w7-207-the-coded-neon-sign", title: "The coded neon sign", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Grim watched a neon sign blink over the club. He read its flashes as a secret warning. Opal, the monkey owner, found him writing dots and lines on a napkin. She showed him a loose wire behind the sign. Grim held the ladder while she fixed it. The sign lit up. It said Open. Grim went inside, ordered bananas, and used the napkin to wipe his muddy shoes before sitting at a table." },
  { id: "w7-005-the-short-cut-race", title: "The short cut race", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Rook raced Tess round the lake. His monkey feet flew while Tess took small steps. He found a short cut through a shed full of bananas and stopped to eat. Tess reached the last bend and sat down. A cart had tipped and blocked the route to the line. Rook came out with a full mouth and helped her shift it. They crossed at once, and shared the prize bench for a nap." },
  { id: "w7-266-the-montage-mop", title: "The montage mop", pay: 231200, lib: 7, text: "Quill trained for the fight in a fast montage. He threw ropes, sacks, and towels across the monkey gym while music played. Quartz stopped the shot when a sack rolled under his foot. They cleaned the floor and filmed a final sweep in the montage. Quill reached the match with a clear space to train. Quartz got a screen credit, and the bananas stayed on a shelf where no flying towel could strike them." },
  { id: "w7-042-the-wishing-well-queue", title: "The wishing well queue", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Wes threw a coin in the well and wished for bananas. Kay, the monkey keeper, fished the coin out to pay for rope. Wes said the wish had gone wrong. Kay showed him the broken bucket. Wes tied his tail to the rope and helped haul water for the fruit trees. A month later they picked a full crop. Kay gave him the first bunch and kept the well free of coins." },
  { id: "w7-123-the-locked-room-window", title: "The locked room window", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Hope locked a room with bananas inside. When she opened it, the fruit was gone. Dan checked the lock, then the ceiling, then his monkey hat. Hope asked why he had not checked the open window. Dan climbed out and found the fruit on a ledge where wind had blown it. He brought it back dry in his hat. Hope shut the window and put a small latch on it before dinner." },
  { id: "w7-136-the-spy-pen-jam", title: "The spy pen jam", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Aura used a pen that could shoot rope, flash light, and play songs. Creek asked her to sign for a parcel of bananas. The monkey pressed the wrong switch and tied the parcel to the desk. Creek lent her a plain pencil. Aura signed, cut the rope, and put the pen back in its case. She used the parcel string to tie a pencil onto the case so it would always be close." },
  { id: "w7-019-the-lake-gives-back-a-spoon", title: "The lake gives back a spoon", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Ari dropped his axe in the lake. Eda rose from the reeds with a gold spoon and asked if it was his. The monkey said no. She brought a silver fork. He said no again. At last she found the axe, stuck in a log beside the bank. Ari freed it with his tail. Eda gave him the spoon for his care. He used it to serve her mashed bananas on shore." },
  { id: "w7-083-the-cheese-cloud", title: "The cheese cloud", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Chase made a cheese cloud for Gem and served it in an empty bowl. The monkey guest sneezed and blew the cloud into the vent. Chase stared at his dish. Gem asked for cheese she could hold. He cut a slice, added bananas, and set it on a plate. She paid the full price. Chase kept the cloud machine for party fog and put a napkin over the vent before his next test." },
  { id: "w7-088-the-golf-sand-picnic", title: "The golf sand picnic", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Glen hit his ball into the sand pit six times. Cora offered the monkey a shorter club, but he wanted to prove his power. His next swing dug a hole beside the ball. Cora spread a cloth over it and opened the bananas. Glen sat down at last. After lunch he used the short club and cleared the sand. Cora raked the pit smooth and kept the long club as a picnic pole." },
  { id: "w7-046-the-rainbow-gate-key", title: "The rainbow gate key", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Wil told Rin that a key lay at the end of the rainbow. Rin crossed fields but the colors moved with her. The monkey came back wet and cross. Wil looked at his own wall and saw the key hung under a rainbow artwork. He had left out that part. Rin opened the garden, picked bananas, and painted a map on the gate. Wil now used that map when he gave advice." },
  { id: "w7-055-the-tiny-pie-slice", title: "The tiny pie slice", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Pam baked one pie for seven judges. Jed said each slice must weigh the same. The monkey used a scale, but crumbs kept falling into her fur. Pam cut the pie into small cubes and gave each judge a bowl. Jed still wanted a grand slice for the photo. Pam shaped his cubes into a wedge and put bananas beside it. He took the photo, then ate the same share as the rest." },
  { id: "w7-076-the-sidekick-map", title: "The sidekick map", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Heath charged into the cave while Sid checked the map. The monkey hero reached a wall and struck a bold pose. Sid found a side door that led to the stolen bananas. Heath tried to claim the rescue, but his cape was still caught on a nail inside. Sid freed him and shared the fruit. Heath gave Sid the map badge and asked him to lead the next mission while he carried bags." },
  { id: "w7-099-the-ice-rink-broom", title: "The ice rink broom", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Sia tried a grand spin on the rink and hit a leaf. Her monkey tail swung out and she sat down hard. Kip offered to sweep before her next turn. Sia took the broom and pushed it while she skated a simple circle. The rink cleared, and she found a steady rhythm. Her final spin worked. Kip gave her bananas, and the broom got a place beside her shiny cup in the display case." },
  { id: "w7-151-the-meeting-to-end-meetings", title: "The meeting to end meetings", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Mabel called a meeting to cut talks. Cole brought a clock and a bag of bananas. Every monkey got one minute to speak, but Mabel used hers to list the agenda. Cole turned the clock round so she could see it. Mabel stopped before the bell. They cut the next meeting and used its hour to fix the loose shelf. Cole put the clock there, with enough space beside it for lunch." },
  { id: "w7-014-the-fox-and-the-low-grapes", title: "The fox and the low grapes", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Fen wore a fox mask and claimed he could reach any fruit. A bunch of grapes hung just above his tail. He said they must taste bad. Ivy, a young monkey, placed a box below the vine and picked one. It was sweet. Fen climbed the box too, but it tipped. Ivy held it still. Fen shared the grapes and traded his mask for a basket that could hold fruit but could not boast." },
  { id: "w7-119-the-spy-boat-oar", title: "The spy boat oar", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Birch leaped into a boat to chase a secret courier. Plum pushed off, then found the oars missing. The monkeys used flat boxes from their lunch as paddles. They reached the other boat at the dock. The courier had brought their oars back from the repair shop. Birch took them and paid with bananas. Plum kept the boxes as spare paddles, after washing all the soft fruit out of their corners." },
  { id: "w7-146-the-moon-rover-picnic-brake", title: "The moon rover picnic brake", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Halo parked the moon rover beside a hill for lunch. It rolled down while the monkey peeled bananas. Iris chased it with a rope and tied it to a rock. Halo found the parking brake loose under his seat. They fixed the bolt, then tested it on a small slope. The rover stayed still. Halo put the rope in the tool box and ate his lunch on flat ground before the next drive." },
  { id: "w7-194-the-time-sheet-tail", title: "The time sheet tail", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Nova made Night record every minute on a time sheet. The monkey spent half an hour noting how long the notes took. Nova asked why filing had slowed. Night showed her the loop of entries about entries. They set one box for the full filing task and one for lunch. Night filled both after work and went home on time. Nova could read the simple sheet in just one minute." },
  { id: "w7-013-the-tiny-giant-hat", title: "The giant shade hat", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Giant Meg wore a hat that hid the sun from the village. Poe, a monkey tailor, climbed its brim to ask her to move. She could not see where her feet went. Poe cut eye holes in the hat, then tied its top with his tail. Meg saw the huts and stepped round them. She paid him with bananas and used the spare cloth to shade the village in hot weather." },
  { id: "w7-016-the-spell-that-kept-time", title: "The spell that kept time", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Mage Lux cast a sleep spell on the hall. Belle stayed awake because she was outside peeling bananas. The monkey cooks slept over cold pans, and no one could serve lunch. Belle wound the old clock and set its bell for noon. The chime woke the hall. Lux said the spell should last years. Belle pointed to the lunch list. He changed it to a nap spell and joined the queue." },
  { id: "w7-094-the-villain-trap-mat", title: "The villain trap mat", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Voss built a pit under a rug to catch Holly. The monkey hero saw that the rug sagged over a hole when her tail brushed it and stepped around it. Voss leaned down to check the edge and fell in himself. Holly lowered a basket of bananas, then a ladder. Voss ate before he climbed out. They filled the pit with soil and planted a tree. Holly kept the rug for the shade beneath it." },
  { id: "w7-190-the-office-smell-survey", title: "The office smell survey", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Kelp sent a survey about a bad smell near the desks. Kit, the monkey cleaner, found a rotten banana beneath the fridge. He removed it before anyone filled the survey out. Kelp still wanted data, so Kit wrote One Old Fruit on the form. The next survey asked if the room smelled better. Kit opened a window and went home. Kelp cut the third survey and added a weekly sweep under the fridge instead." },
  { id: "w7-048-the-rescue-ladder-rental", title: "The rescue ladder rental", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Plum offered a prize to anyone who could reach her balcony. Noel rode up with a ladder, but every knight wanted to borrow it. The monkey charged one banana each and watched them climb. Plum came down the same ladder to join the queue for snacks. She gave Noel the prize for making a safe route. He used it to buy more ladders, and Plum ran the desk that lent them out." },
  { id: "w7-058-the-salad-trophy", title: "The salad trophy", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Sage made a salad in the shape of a trophy. Jay gave the monkey a real trophy for it. Sage tried to eat that one and found it much too hard. Jay said prizes were for shelves. Sage had no shelf, only a small hut full of bananas. He traded the trophy for seeds and grew a garden. At the next contest he served bowls and asked for an empty sack as his prize." },
  { id: "w7-121-the-missing-pie-rim", title: "The missing pie rim", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Dex looked for a stolen pie. Bina showed him a pie dish with just a ring of crust left. The monkey found crumbs on his own tail. He had sat on the sill deep in thought and eaten the pie there. Dex paid Bina in bananas, then helped bake a new one. He closed the case with a plain note about his snack. Bina served him lunch before she hired him for another search." },
  { id: "w7-154-the-growth-chart-roof", title: "The growth chart roof", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Faye showed a chart where sales rose through the roof. Ash checked the scale and found it counted peels instead of bananas. The monkey founder had called every peel a new client. Ash weighed the actual fruit and drew a smaller chart. Faye first frowned, then saw that the stock would last a week. They sold the peels as compost and counted that money once. The new chart fit neatly on one page." },
  { id: "w7-021-the-tower-has-stairs", title: "The tower has stairs", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Rae lived in a tower and let down her long tail when Prince Cal came. He climbed halfway, then sneezed from her fur. Rae hauled him in and showed him the stairs behind a curtain. The monkeys had missed them for years because the curtain said Keep Out. Cal took the sign down. Rae opened a stair cafe and sold bananas at each landing. Cal used the lift, which was a plain bucket." },
  { id: "w7-024-the-wish-fish-dinner", title: "The wish fish dinner", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Fae caught a fish that offered wishes. It was Milo, a monkey in a blue suit, hiding from his dish chores. Fae wished for a grand meal. Milo led her home and cooked beans with bananas. She wished for clean plates. He sighed and washed them with his tail wrapped round the brush. Her last wish was for him to join her at the table. He did, still damp, and ate his share." },
  { id: "w7-044-the-straw-gold-label", title: "The straw gold label", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Ian offered to spin straw into gold if Sal guessed his name. Sal, a monkey with a seed shop, asked why anyone wanted gold straw. Ian said it sold well for nest trim. Sal painted a bundle yellow and labeled it Plain Straw. Birds bought that instead. Ian told her his name without a guess and asked for work. She paid him bananas to paint labels, where his fine small brush proved useful." },
  { id: "w7-251-the-sitcom-door-key", title: "The sitcom door key", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Alf burst into the flat every day for the sitcom. Nell finally changed the lock. The monkey actor stood outside while the laugh track played to no one. He knocked and asked to come in. Nell opened the door and offered bananas. The scene worked better with one real pause. Alf kept a knock in every later script, and Nell could finish her tea before his daily grand entry began." },
  { id: "w7-062-the-slow-sprint-camera", title: "The slow sprint camera", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Rue trained for the sprint, but the race camera could see only tails. Every monkey curled a tail over the line before their feet arrived. Judge Finn could not choose a winner. Rue set a second line behind the first and asked each runner to touch it with a foot. They raced again without tricks. Rue came third and won bananas for fixing the rules. Finn used the tail photo as a funny poster." },
  { id: "w7-073-the-mighty-jar-lid", title: "The mighty jar lid", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Hugo could lift a bridge, but he could not open a jam jar. Cat watched the monkey strain until his fur stood up. She tapped the lid with a spoon and ran warm water round its rim. Hugo turned it with one finger. He ate jam on bananas, then asked to learn the trick. Cat made him wash the spoon first. Hugo added a small tap move to his list of great powers." },
  { id: "w7-085-the-food-critic-fork", title: "The food critic fork", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Cliff gave Cia low marks because her fork was bent. The monkey cook bent it back, but the critic found a dent in the spoon. Cia set a bowl of bananas beside him without any metal tools. Cliff ate with his hands and forgot to grumble. He wrote that the meal had a fine rustic style. Cia framed the review next to the tool rack, where the bent fork held spare towels." },
  { id: "w7-212-the-high-noon-shade", title: "The high noon shade", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Sunny called Rust to a duel at noon. Both monkeys stood in the dust with dry mouths and hot fur. Rust asked if they could settle the cattle fence dispute under a tree. Sunny agreed. They drew the field border in the shade and split the cost of a new gate. No shots fired. They ate bananas at one, then spent two hours fitting hinges while the sun moved off the road." },
  { id: "w7-117-the-decoder-drum", title: "The decoder drum", pay: 234600, lib: 7, text: "Rue heard taps through the wall and thought a spy sent a code. The monkey wrote each beat down, then fed the marks into his decoder. It said Bring Bananas. Min opened the next door with a drum under her arm. She was playing a new tune. Rue brought fruit anyway and asked her to play it again. His decoder made a fine beat clock once he stopped asking it to read secret notes." },
  { id: "w7-111-the-spy-peel-code", title: "The spy peel code", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Ace wrote a code on a banana peel. Ada ate the fruit, then tossed the peel into the bin. The monkey agents needed the code to open a safe. Ace fetched the peel with his tail and read it upside down. The safe opened to show six clean plates. Ada set the table while Ace copied the code onto paper. They ate more bananas and put every new peel into the compost box." },
  { id: "w7-210-the-fog-ferry-bill", title: "The fog ferry bill", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Frost chased a shadow onto the ferry without paying. Tide stopped the boat and asked for his fare. The monkey sleuth pointed at the shadow, but it came from a coat on the rail. Frost paid and helped Tide haul the coat in before it blew away. A guest claimed it at the far dock. Frost ate bananas on the ride back and kept his ticket visible in the brim of his hat." },
  { id: "w7-038-the-mermaid-dry-seat", title: "The mermaid dry seat", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Mira wore a fish tail in the lake show. She wished to sit on land, but the tail made each chair tip. Sailor Sid brought a stool with a slot for it. The monkey slid in and ate bananas without falling. Mira kept the fish tail for shows and her own tail for walks. Sid put wheels on the stool so she could roll from the lake to lunch in one smooth trip." },
  { id: "w7-057-the-spoon-draft", title: "The spoon draft", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Cal picked cooks by how fast they could stir. Sue used her tail and won a place on the monkey team. In the final, the soup needed slow care. The fast cooks spilled it onto their fur. Sue tied a bell to her spoon and kept it quiet. Cal made the team follow her pace. They served smooth soup with bananas and put the silent spoon above the cup they had won." },
  { id: "w7-054-the-secret-sauce-jar", title: "The secret sauce jar", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Cora would not share her secret sauce with Aunt Ann. She hid the jar in a hollow stump. A monkey troop mistook it for glue and used it on a kite. Cora found the kite stuck to the tree, with a smell of bananas. Ann helped soak the joints in warm water. Cora wrote the sauce name on a fresh jar and gave Ann the recipe. The kite flew after lunch with no sticky tail." },
  { id: "w7-256-the-talent-show-tail", title: "The talent show tail", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Fia sang well, but Fern wanted a bigger finish. The monkey tied ribbons to her tail and spun while holding the final note. She grew dizzy and forgot the words. Fern gave her water and asked for a simple song. Fia sat on a stool and sang it cleanly. The crowd sat still, then cheered. Fern gave her a plain mic and bananas as the prize, leaving the loose ribbons for the stage curtain." },
  { id: "w7-035-the-old-dog-mask", title: "The old dog mask", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Don said he was too old to learn new tricks. Pat tied a dog mask over his monkey face and asked him to fetch a stick. Don refused until the stick held a bunch of bananas. He brought it back with his tail. Pat tried that too and fell on his nose. Don taught him how to curl his tail first. Pat gave him the fruit and asked for a slower lesson next time." },
  { id: "w7-047-the-crown-itch", title: "The crown itch", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Pax put on a cursed crown and felt an awful itch. Wye said only a rare herb could end it. The monkey prince took off the crown to scratch his fur. The itch stopped. Wye found rough wire inside the rim and blushed. She padded it with wool. Pax wore it for the feast, then hung it on a hook. He paid Wye in bananas for the pad and skipped the herb quest." },
  { id: "w7-068-the-bowling-tail-lane", title: "The bowling tail lane", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Belle rolled balls with her tail to impress the crowd. One ball curved into the snack stand and crushed the bananas. Lane Lee closed her lane until she learned to aim. The monkey used soft balls and empty cups in the yard. By dusk she could hit one cup at a time. Belle swept the snack stand, made a fresh fruit mash, and rolled a plain strike with both hands the next day." },
  { id: "w7-091-the-rescue-robot-spoon", title: "The rescue robot spoon", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Bolt built Hilda a robot that could carry any spoon. Hilda wanted it to rescue a cart full of bananas. The machine brought her one spoon and sat down. The monkey hero tied the spoon to a rope, hooked the cart axle, and pulled. Bolt saw his robot needed a broader job list. He taught it to hold rope next. Hilda kept the spoon in her kit because it had already earned its place." },
  { id: "w7-126-the-bell-tower-whisper", title: "The bell tower whisper", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Della heard low voices in the bell tower and went up to face a ghost. Kian, a monkey keeper, stood below with a basket of bananas. Della found a pipe that carried his voice to the top. He had asked if she wanted lunch. She spoke into the pipe and asked for two bananas. Kian sent them up in a bucket. Della labeled the pipe Lunch Call and left the ghosts out of her report." },
  { id: "w7-114-the-briefcase-picnic", title: "The briefcase picnic", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Fern left a case on the park bench for Fay. A gust blew it open, and bananas rolled across the path. The monkey agents crawled after them as if they had to inspect the paving stones. Fay caught the last fruit with her tail. They sat down and ate because the case had held only lunch. Fern put a latch on it before the next swap. Fay brought a cloth to cover the bench." },
  { id: "w7-177-the-mute-button-tail", title: "The mute button tail", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Briar asked Bri to give a report on the call. The monkey spoke for ten minutes with her mic off. Each peer waved a tail at the screen, but Bri thought they liked her speech. Briar held up a card that said No Sound. Bri turned the mic on and gave one clear line with the sales total. The call ended early. Briar kept the card on his desk beside the mute switch." },
  { id: "w7-182-the-office-trophy-cupboard", title: "The office trophy cupboard", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Dove gave Dune a trophy each month for tidy work. Soon the awards filled the shelf where the monkey kept his tools. Dune put the awards in a cabinet and asked for no more. Dove said praise should be visible. Dune showed him the clean desk and the files in order. Dove gave him a day off instead. Dune cleaned one small cup before leaving and used it to hold his best pens." },
  { id: "w7-184-the-calendar-chair-block", title: "The calendar chair block", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Flora booked every chair in the planner so her team would have space. Finch arrived alone and found the monkey hall empty but fully booked. He sat on the floor to mend a file box. Flora came in and tripped over his tail. Finch showed her the unused chairs. She cleared all but the two needed for a call. Finch sat at last, and the file box stayed safely beneath the desk." },
  { id: "w7-278-the-poetry-slam-whisper", title: "The poetry slam whisper", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Haze wrote a poem about a lost spoon. Heath told the monkey to shout it to win the slam. Haze tried, but her voice broke before the last line. She asked for a quiet reading instead. The room hushed, and guests heard where the spoon had gone, into the banana mash. Haze pulled it from the prop bowl at the end. Heath gave her the prize for the clear story, not the volume." },
  { id: "w7-028-the-crane-lunch", title: "The crane lunch", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Flo served soup on flat plates, though Kai had a long paper beak for the play. Kai planned revenge with tall jars. The monkey cooks stopped when both spilled soup on their fur. Flo found wide cups and Kai took his beak off. They ate in peace, then used the jars for flowers. Their guests brought bananas and asked to keep the plates, which made fine hats for the next play." },
  { id: "w7-033-the-twelve-dancing-tails", title: "The twelve dancing tails", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Pia and her sisters wore out their shoes each night. Guard Glen hid by the door to find out why. The monkeys used the shoes as drums while their tails danced. Pia feared the king would ban the noise. Glen lined the soles with soft moss and helped them set a quiet beat. The king slept well, the shoes lasted, and Glen got bananas for his first lesson in tail dance." },
  { id: "w7-080-the-hero-fan-club-queue", title: "The hero fan club queue", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Hero spent all day signing cards while Fenn waited at the end of the line. A monkey shouted that a branch blocked the road. Hero feared the fans would leave if he stepped away from his desk. Fenn took the pen and signed a card that said Back Soon. Hero moved the branch and brought bananas for the queue. Fenn got the first card when he came back, with a real leaf on it." },
  { id: "w7-124-the-vanishing-ink-list", title: "The vanishing ink list", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Dawn saw blank pages where Chet had written the meal list. The monkey sleuth blamed secret ink. She warmed a page over the stove, but no words came back. Chet showed her the sponge he had used to wipe sauce off the book. He had wiped the pencil too. Dawn wrote a fresh list on a board. Chet hung it above the sink, and they ate the bananas the old list had omitted." },
  { id: "w7-139-the-night-vision-lamp", title: "The night vision lamp", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Dusk wore night goggles to enter a dark hall. Gray turned a lamp on, and the monkey agent saw only glare. Dusk took the goggles off and found Gray holding his lost bag of bananas. There was no secret vault, just the coat room. Dusk thanked him and checked the room number on his note. He went to the next door with plain eyes and left the goggles in their padded case." },
  { id: "w7-192-the-bonus-fruit-scale", title: "The bonus fruit scale", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Marsh paid bonuses by fruit weight. Mari got a bunch of green bananas, while senior staff got soft ripe ones. The monkey weighed her share and found it heavier but too hard to eat. She brought a ripe bunch to compare. Marsh tested a slice of each and saw the problem. He let workers choose when to collect their fruit. Mari waited three days and got a ripe bunch at the same fair weight." },
  { id: "w7-201-the-raincoat-clue", title: "The raincoat clue", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Slate stood in the rain to look grim while Coral waited indoors. The monkey sleuth soaked his notes and could no longer read the address of her missing cart. Coral gave him a towel and drew the route on the back of a dry bill. Slate traced it to the shed next door. The cart sat under a tarp, full of bananas. He wheeled it back and wrote his report by a warm stove." },
  { id: "w7-255-the-soap-opera-letter", title: "The soap opera letter", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Enid found a letter that could settle the plot. Echo urged the monkey to hide it until the next season. Enid read it aloud instead. It was a receipt for bananas, not a secret wedding. Echo stared at the wrong prop in her hand. The crew found the right letter beneath a cup and shot the scene again. Enid put all letters in marked trays, so a lunch bill could never run the plot twice." },
  { id: "w7-027-the-proud-pond-swan", title: "The proud pond swan", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Dax wore a duck cap to fit in at the pond. Swan Sue said his brown fur spoiled the flock photo. The monkey took his cap off and held it over the lens as a shade. The glare went away. Sue saw that the photo looked much better. She asked Dax to stand beside her for a new one. He did, with bananas in his cap, and every bird leaned toward the snack." },
  { id: "w7-070-the-coach-chalk-storm", title: "The coach chalk storm", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Craig filled a board with arrows for the final play. Pia could not see which way to run. The monkey coach wiped half the lines away, then half again. Only one arrow stayed. Pia ran that way and found a basket of bananas beside the field. Craig had drawn on the lunch map by mistake. They ate, then drew the play on the proper board. Pia scored before the chalk dust settled." },
  { id: "w7-132-the-starship-tail-seat", title: "The starship tail seat", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Beck made a ship seat with no tail hole. Pearl sat in it and could not reach the buttons. The monkey builder cut a slot, but loose foam clogged the air vent. Pearl held a bag under the seat while Beck brushed the foam out. They tested each switch before takeoff. The ship flew well, and Pearl ate bananas in comfort. Beck added tail slots to every seat on his plan that evening." },
  { id: "w7-135-the-space-suit-sneeze", title: "The space suit sneeze", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Petal sneezed inside her space suit and could not wipe her nose. Mica told the monkey to come into the air lock before taking her helmet off. Petal waited through the slow cycle, then found a feather stuck to her fur. Mica removed it and cleaned the glass. Petal kept bananas outside the suit for lunch. Her next walk went well, with no feather and a clear view of each moon rock." },
  { id: "w7-149-the-vanished-picnic-blanket", title: "The vanished picnic blanket", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Lila set bananas on a blanket and went for cups. The blanket was gone before she came back. Lake checked the monkey yard and saw a square patch of shade under a tree. The wind had lifted the blanket into its limbs. Lake climbed up while Lila held a basket below. The fruit fell safely into it. They tied stones to each corner of the blanket and ate their picnic beneath the same tree." },
  { id: "w7-205-the-noir-coffee-spoon", title: "The noir coffee spoon", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Smoke took his coffee black and cold to look tough. Wren saw the monkey shiver and added hot water. Smoke argued until his tail stopped shaking. He finally asked for a spoon and milk. Wren served bananas with the cup. Smoke solved the case of a missing coat while he warmed up, finding it on the hook behind him. He left a fair tip and wore the coat on the rainy walk home." },
  { id: "w7-219-the-cactus-fence-gap", title: "The cactus fence gap", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Thorn planted cactus along his border. Moss could no longer bring bananas through to the shared market. The monkey rivals argued until Thorn caught his own tail on a spine. Moss trimmed a clear path and helped pull the thorn out. They built one gate between the cactus rows. Thorn kept his fence, Moss kept the route, and both could carry crates without needing thick rugs over their fur on every trip." },
  { id: "w7-036-the-donkey-song-ban", title: "The donkey song ban", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Dot sang so loudly that the town asked her to leave. She was a monkey in a donkey hood and took the news badly. Mayor Max heard her voice shake loose ripe bananas from a high tree. He hired her to sing in the grove each morning. Dot could now choose any song she liked. The town slept late, the fruit crew wore ear plugs, and the hood became a sack for the crop." },
  { id: "w7-052-the-soup-whistle", title: "The soup whistle", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Cleo asked for silence in her soup shop. Pip slurped once and got sent outside. The young monkey heard the pot whistle behind him. Cleo ran out to scold the sound, but Pip pointed at the stove. The pot was too full. He held a bowl while she poured some out. They added bananas to cool it. Cleo put a bell by the door and let guests ring it for more soup." },
  { id: "w7-093-the-rocket-boots-brake", title: "The rocket boots brake", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Harry wore rocket boots to reach fires fast. He flew past a smoky shed and landed in a pond. Mox pulled the monkey out by his tail. The boots had a start button but no brake. Mox added one and made Harry train on the grass. The next smoke came from a grill. Harry stopped beside it, brought water for the cook, and stayed to eat bananas while the boots cooled in the shade." },
  { id: "w7-106-the-gravity-switch-snack", title: "The gravity switch snack", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Sol turned gravity down to clean beneath his desk. Gem came in with bananas, and the fruit floated to the roof. The monkey guests chased it with their tails but could not reach. Sol tied a spoon to a cord and hooked each bunch down. He turned gravity back up before serving lunch. Gem asked for a plain broom next time. Sol kept the cord, which also pulled dust from behind the shelf." },
  { id: "w7-128-the-map-false-fold", title: "The map false fold", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Demi dug beneath an old tree where the map showed a cross. Gil saw that the map had folded over on itself. The monkey hunters opened it flat and found the cross marked a tool shed. Inside lay a note that told them to dig by the river. They found a chest of bananas there, left by the camp cook. Demi ate one and put the map in a stiff frame for the walk home." },
  { id: "w7-053-the-cake-tower-brace", title: "The cake tower brace", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Baz stacked cakes taller than his head. Hope asked how he would cut them for the judges. The monkey pushed his tail through the middle as a brace, which made the top cake tilt. Hope slid small plates beneath each layer. Baz served a whole row of flat cakes instead. The judges could taste them all without ladders. Baz put a tiny ladder beside one cake and won the prize for best tower." },
  { id: "w7-150-the-case-of-the-extra-tail", title: "The case of the extra tail", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Alder walked into the hall with two tails. Laurel feared a strange spell. The monkey actor showed her one tail, then the other, both moving in time. She asked him to turn round. A string led from the false tail to his wrist. Alder was testing a costume for a two headed beast. Laurel helped hide the string under his fur. They ate bananas after the test, and the spare tail became a curtain tie." },
  { id: "w7-178-the-password-fruit-bowl", title: "The password fruit bowl", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Beryl made Birch choose a new code each morning. The monkey wrote them on banana peels because he had no spare paper. At lunch he forgot which peel had the current code and could not open his desk. Beryl helped him sort them by color. They chose one strong code and put it in a safe record book. Birch threw the peels into compost and stopped storing office keys beside his lunch." },
  { id: "w7-018-the-flute-with-one-note", title: "The flute with one note", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Hal said his flute would rid the town of pests. He could play only one note. The monkeys came out to ask him to stop. Mayor Liv saw their tails twitch at each squeak and had an idea. She put them in a line to sweep the street in time. Hal played until each crumb was gone. The pests left for lack of food, and Hal earned bananas for a short song." },
  { id: "w7-043-the-hare-alarm-clock", title: "The hare alarm clock", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Hank took a nap during the race and set an alarm in his fur. Ty walked past, heard it ring, and thought a monkey needed help. He woke Hank, who sprang up and ran the wrong way. Ty called him back to the trail. They came in late, after the prize bananas had gone soft. Hank mashed them into cake. Ty cut two large slices and they ate beneath the silent clock." },
  { id: "w7-116-the-spy-clock-fast", title: "The spy clock fast", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Reed raced to the tower before noon to stop a secret trade. The monkey arrived early and found no one but Wren mending clocks. His watch was an hour fast. Wren fixed it while Reed shared his bananas. At noon a cart came to swap old clocks for new ones. Reed checked its permit and let it pass. He sent a report about the false alarm, with the correct time on every page." },
  { id: "w7-152-the-desk-hot-spot", title: "The desk hot spot", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Mina chose hot desks by daily vote. Wade got the desk beside the stove and singed his monkey fur. Mina said hot meant shared, but Wade asked for a cooler spot. They rolled the desk to the window and marked seats with clips instead of heat. Wade hung bananas from his clip during lunch. Mina banned food on desks, then took one because she had not brought a snack of her own." },
  { id: "w7-017-a-shoe-shop-for-elves", title: "A shoe shop for elves", pay: 238000, lib: 7, text: "Dex left leather out for elves to sew at night. Ona, a monkey in an elf cap, made six shoes, but all had holes for tails. Dex found them useless until rain flooded the lane. He wore one on his tail and kept his fur dry. He sold the rest as tail boots. Ona got fair pay in bananas, and Dex moved the sewing shift to day so she could sleep." },
  { id: "w7-067-the-mascot-penalty", title: "The mascot penalty", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Moe wore a giant banana suit to cheer the team. His monkey tail dragged behind and tripped Cass near the goal. The referee sent Moe to the bench. Moe cut a hole for his tail, then made small flags from the spare cloth. He waved them from his seat and kept score with bananas. Cass scored twice. Moe gave the team the fruit and folded the suit into a tidy bag for the flags." },
  { id: "w7-060-the-rolling-pin-baton", title: "The rolling pin baton", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Bea gave Ren a rolling pin for the kitchen relay. Ren raced so fast that dough wrapped round his monkey tail. He reached the next table with no dough left on the tray. Bea dusted his tail with flour and rolled it over the sheet. The dough came off in a neat spiral. They baked it with bananas inside. The judges asked for the recipe, so Bea drew a tail beside the rolling pin." },
  { id: "w7-074-the-hidden-hero-badge", title: "The hidden hero badge", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Hen changed into her hero suit behind the fruit stall. Fay saw her tail under the curtain and knew at once. The monkey begged her to keep the secret. Fay agreed, but the suit had no room for the bananas Hen had just bought. Fay lent her a plain bag. Hen saved a kite from a roof and came home with the fruit. Fay kept the badge safe while Hen washed the dusty suit." },
  { id: "w7-125-the-clue-under-the-hat", title: "The clue under the hat", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Dale found a key beside the empty fruit box. He hid it in his hat, then checked the room for hours. Ari asked the monkey to take a break and brush his fur. The key fell onto the desk. It opened the box in the next room, where all the bananas sat safe from ants. Dale thanked Ari and made a tray for clues. His hat held only his head on the next case." },
  { id: "w7-295-the-album-cover-soup", title: "The album cover soup", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Dawn chose a cover showing a bowl of soup for her album of love songs. Dell asked the monkey how it linked to the music. Dawn said the colors matched her fur. Dell played the songs and drew two tails linked instead. Dawn liked that better and kept the soup picture for a recipe card. The album sold well. Dell ate bananas at the launch and gave guests the soup card as a useful extra." },
  { id: "w7-032-the-magic-pot-lid", title: "The magic pot lid", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Mel gave Penny a pot that made hot oats on command. Penny forgot the stop word, and oats filled the monkey hut. She slid the lid under the stream and used it as a chute to the yard. Friends came with bowls and bananas. Mel came back to find a feast in the yard. He said the stop word was Enough. Penny carved it on the lid, then asked for one last small bowl." },
  { id: "w7-071-the-cape-caught-in-the-bus", title: "The cape caught in the bus", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Hal leaped onto the bus to save it from a loose wheel. His cape caught in the door, leaving the monkey stuck on the step. Di stopped the bus and freed him. Hal used the cape to wipe grease off the axle while Di fixed the bolt. They drove to the shop at walking speed. The riders paid Hal with bananas. He cut his cape short and kept a wrench in the hem." },
  { id: "w7-009-the-trail-of-shells", title: "The trail of shells", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Lark and Reed left bits of banana on the path to mark their way home. Birds ate the bits. The young monkeys reached a pond and saw no trail. Reed cracked nuts and placed the shells in pairs on stones. Lark climbed a tree to spot their roof. They laid more shells on the path toward it and came home at dusk. Next day they took a map and kept the bananas for lunch." },
  { id: "w7-015-the-red-cloak-laundry", title: "The red cloak laundry", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Ren took soup to Aunt Uma in her bright red cloak. Wes, a monkey in a wolf mask, tried to lure her down a dark path. Ren knew him by the strip of fur near his nose. She asked him to carry the soup while she washed her cloak in the stream. He waited so long that he got hungry. At the hut they shared soup and bananas, and he hung up his mask." },
  { id: "w7-040-the-seven-soup-bowls", title: "The seven soup bowls", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Sia found seven bowls in a small hut and filled them with soup. Dell came home with six other monkeys, all in dwarf hats. They had meant the bowls for paint. Sia offered to wash them, but Dell tasted the soup and asked her to stay. They painted the hut after lunch. Sia used mashed bananas to make yellow paint for the door, which smelled so good that bees came to visit." },
  { id: "w7-077-the-moon-base-broom", title: "The moon base broom", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Haze built a secret base on the moon. Clio came to clean it and found dust in every crack. The monkey hero had no broom, only a ray gun. Clio taped dry leaves to the gun and swept the floor. Haze tried to fire it, but Clio took out the power cell first. They packed bananas in the clean kitchen. Haze made a chore chart and put his own name on the first shift." },
  { id: "w7-108-the-invisible-ship-ticket", title: "The invisible ship ticket", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Pea hid her ship with a cloak beam to avoid the port fee. Gil, a monkey guard, heard her tail drag down the ramp. He put a ticket on the empty air. Pea could not find it until she turned the beam off. She paid the fee in bananas and asked for a visible parking post. Gil gave her one. Pea left the beam off at the port and found her ship without bruised toes." },
  { id: "w7-118-the-stealth-squeak", title: "The stealth squeak", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Vale wore silent shoes for a night mission. His monkey tail creaked against the shiny floor instead. May heard him from the shop and handed him a cloth. Vale wrapped his tail, crossed the hall, and found the lost key beside the sink. May had left it there while washing bananas. Vale gave it back, then removed his shoes. His bare feet were quiet enough, and the cloth became his regular tail towel." },
  { id: "w7-020-the-bear-chair-repair", title: "The bear chair repair", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Goldie tried each chair in the bear hut. She was a monkey guest, but had lost her invite in the wind. One chair broke beneath her tail. Bear Ben came home and found her mending it with rope. He read the invite that stuck to his boot. The chair was his gift to her, though he had built it too small. They made a wider seat and ate bananas while the glue dried." },
  { id: "w7-092-the-x-ray-lunchbox", title: "The x ray lunchbox", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Hex used his x ray gaze to check a sealed box at the gate. He saw long curved shapes and cried that it held secret weapons. Gage opened the box to show bananas. The monkey hero blushed beneath his mask. Gage asked him to read the label before using his gift. Hex checked the next box and found towels. He carried both boxes to the hall and used plain sight to serve lunch." },
  { id: "w7-112-the-hat-bug", title: "The hat bug", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Ash put a tiny sound bug in the hat of Clerk Clay. The monkey clerk lent his hat to a fruit seller, so Ash heard only prices all day. He went to fetch the bug and found it stuck to a bunch of bananas. Clay helped him take it off with a spoon. Ash paid for the damaged fruit. His report said the market had fresh stock, which was true and useful to the cook." },
  { id: "w7-265-the-sequel-spare-door", title: "The sequel spare door", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Pine wanted the broken door left hanging so a sequel could use it. Pax saw the hinge wobble over the monkey crew. He propped the door safely and asked to film a repair scene. Pine agreed, though he feared it would end the story. The viewers liked seeing the hero finish the job. Pax carried the spare hinge home, and Pine planned a new sequel about a new door instead of leaving this one unsafe." },
  { id: "w7-059-the-burnt-toast-portrait", title: "The burnt toast portrait", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Tom called his burnt toast a bold new dish. Gia took one bite and coughed black dust onto her fur. The monkey chef said that was the style. Gia scraped the toast and used the dark bits to draw his face on a plate. Tom laughed, then made fresh toast at low heat. He served it with bananas and put her art on the menu. The new dish was called Take Your Time." },
  { id: "w7-064-the-pool-lane-knot", title: "The pool lane knot", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Sid tied his tail to a float so he could rest between laps. During the race it caught the lane rope. The monkey kept going in one small circle. Ref Rae halted the race and cut the knot. Sid used the float to hold bananas at the pool edge instead. He swam the full course with a free tail. Rae gave him a plain ribbon and kept the shears close for the next event." },
  { id: "w7-239-the-bailiff-lost-gavel", title: "The bailiff lost gavel", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Iris lost the gavel just before court. Ivy refused to begin without it. The monkey bailiff checked every drawer and found only bananas. Ivy tapped a wooden handle on her desk while she waited. Iris pointed at the head beneath the papers. It was the gavel she had held all morning. Ivy cleared her desk and began the case. Iris put a small tray beside her hand, clearly marked for the gavel alone." },
  { id: "w7-022-the-king-has-pockets", title: "The king has pockets", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Opal sold King Ned a suit that no one could see. Ned walked out in his fur and asked where to put his keys. The monkey weaver offered a bag. Ned asked why he had paid for a suit with no pockets. Opal gave back the bananas and sewed him a plain coat. At the parade Ned held up each pocket for the crowd. They cheered the coat because it could hold their lost keys." },
  { id: "w7-101-the-moon-lunch-leak", title: "The moon lunch leak", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Pax flew to the moon with a crate of bananas. Cora found a leak in the food bag and called the monkey pilot back to the cabin. He patched it with his mission badge, but now no one could read his name. Cora wrote it on his helmet in sauce. They landed safely and shared lunch beside the ship. Pax kept the stained helmet as proof that the cook had saved the trip." },
  { id: "w7-122-the-muddy-paw-clue", title: "The muddy paw clue", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Dot found muddy prints by the empty banana shelf. She accused Gale, whose monkey feet were always dirty. Gale showed her a fresh broom he had used to clean the shed. Dot swept the floor and found a loose wheel track under the prints. The fruit cart had rolled away through the open gate. They fetched it as a team. Dot washed her own muddy feet before writing the report and sharing the bananas." },
  { id: "w7-131-the-alien-lunch-stars", title: "The alien lunch stars", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Tia gave Pine a sealed alien cube. The monkey pilot opened it and found six bananas, each wrapped in foil. He thought the foil was a rare space metal. Tia said it was just there to keep lunch fresh. Pine folded it into stars and hung them in his cabin. He sent Tia a thank you note and gave the empty cube back. She filled it again, this time with a spoon beside the fruit." },
  { id: "w7-284-the-jazz-solo-map", title: "The jazz solo map", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Nix strayed so far from the melody that Nell could not follow. The monkey drummer held a steady beat while Nix looked for the chorus. At last Nell tapped the opening phrase on a small bell. Nix heard it and joined the song again. They wrote the key changes on one card for the next show. After the set they ate bananas, and Nix kept the bell close as a simple way back home." },
  { id: "w7-290-the-portrait-sitter-banana", title: "The portrait sitter banana", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Thorn asked Thyme to hold one pose for hours. The monkey sitter gripped bananas until the fruit went soft. Thorn liked the solemn face, but Thyme was simply hungry. They paused for lunch and swapped the fruit with a wooden model. Thyme held it lightly while Thorn did the picture. The face now looked calm. Thorn listed breaks in his next booking, and Thyme took the real fruit home without another bruise." },
  { id: "w7-185-the-fire-drill-form", title: "The fire drill form", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Fern told Fox to fill a drill form before leaving the hall. The monkey clerk smelled smoke from the toaster and took the troop outside first. Fern carried the blank forms after him. They counted all staff by the gate, then called the kitchen crew. A burnt bun was the only loss. Fox filled the form in the yard. Fern moved the pen box outside so the next safe exit could stay clear." },
  { id: "w7-191-the-printer-jam-chart", title: "The printer jam chart", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Linden drew a chart to explain why the printer jammed. Lilac opened its tray and found a twig inside. The monkey clerk pulled it out with her tail and printed the chart. Linden studied the page, which blamed low morale. Lilac taped the twig over those words. He laughed and rewrote the cause as Wood In Tray. They posted the new chart beside the machine and kept all plant pots on a second shelf." },
  { id: "w7-223-the-vault-echo-rehearsal", title: "The vault echo rehearsal", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Echo tried his vault speech in a tunnel. Ember heard each word through the vent by the monkey guard desk. She came down with a map and showed Echo where the sound went. Echo gave up the theft plan and offered a tunnel tour instead. Ember checked the route and sold tickets for daytime visits. Echo earned bananas from guests who liked the echo. He kept all talks away from the old vault wall." },
  { id: "w7-233-the-jury-lunch-lock", title: "The jury lunch lock", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Cedar sent the jury to a locked room to decide the case. Clover found bananas on the table but no water. The monkey juror knocked until the clerk came. Cedar feared they wanted help with the verdict. Clover held up an empty cup. The clerk brought a jug and opened the side kitchen. The jury did its work with clear heads. Cedar kept a small needs list beside the rules for every later session." },
  { id: "w7-294-the-stage-sword-sponge", title: "The stage sword of foam", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Cedar swung a metal sword and knocked a lamp off the stage. Cora caught it before the monkey could begin his next move. She made a foam sword and painted it gray. Cedar tried the same fight slowly, keeping well clear of the lights. The viewers saw a grand duel, but every strike was soft. Cora stored the real sword in a locked rack and used the spare foam to line the box of prop bananas." },
  { id: "w7-157-the-office-quiet-jar", title: "The office quiet jar", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Bea charged a coin when someone made noise. Creek dropped a mug and owed three coins for the crash. The monkey asked how to report a fire under the quiet rule. Bea opened her mouth, then shut it. Creek put a bell beside the jar and offered one free ring for urgent news. Bea agreed and gave back the coins. They filled the jar with bananas instead, though each peel made a small rustle at lunch." },
  { id: "w7-089-the-referee-ribbon-maze", title: "The referee ribbon maze", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Rex tied ribbons across the track to mark each rule. Rose could not see a clear way through. The monkey referee blew his whistle when her tail touched one ribbon, then tripped on another himself. Rose helped untie them and laid one ribbon along the outside edge. Rex kept the rules on a card in his pocket. The race began late, but all the bananas stayed on the prize table until it ended." },
  { id: "w7-129-the-missing-shadow", title: "The missing shadow", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Dora woke with no shadow and feared a spell. Lyle checked the monkey room and found lamps on every wall. Their light hid the dark patch behind her feet. He turned all but one lamp off. Dora saw her shadow stretch across the floor. She fed Lyle bananas for his help, then asked him to move the lamps into the garden. Her night party had bright paths, and each guest kept a shadow." },
  { id: "w7-148-the-spy-bubble-trail", title: "The spy bubble trail", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Mist wore soap shoes to slide quietly across the hall. Each step left bubbles behind the monkey spy. Maple traced the trail and found him under a desk, peeling bananas. Mist said he was testing a stealth route. Maple gave him a mop and helped dry the floor. They were done before anyone slipped. Mist swapped the soap with soft felt and tested one quiet step at a time, while Maple looked for new trails." },
  { id: "w7-159-the-memo-margin-war", title: "The memo margin war", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Wren wrote a memo about a broken tap. Eve changed its margins six times. The monkey writer watched water drip onto a crate of bananas while the page passed back and forth. Wren took a wrench to the tap and stopped the leak. Eve cleared the seventh margin just as he was done. Wren sent a one line note that said Fixed. Eve kept it on her desk because no one needed to edit its shape." },
  { id: "w7-298-the-award-speech-clock", title: "The award speech clock", pay: 241400, lib: 7, text: "Grove thanked every monkey he had ever met in his award speech. Gilda saw the hall clock pass twelve while his list still grew. She handed him a card with five blank lines. Grove chose the names from this film and closed with one clear thanks to the crew. The crowd clapped at last. Gilda served bananas before all guests left, and Grove sent the other thanks by letter in the morning." },
  { id: "w7-160-the-break-room-spoon-vote", title: "The break room spoon vote", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Cedar asked for a spoon in the break room. Brook formed a panel to choose its shape. The monkeys met for weeks while their soup grew cold. Cedar carved a spoon from a fallen branch and ate lunch. Brook asked if it met the new policy. Cedar handed him a bowl of bananas and the spoon. Brook used it without reading the policy. The panel closed, and the branch gave them three more spoons for the drawer." },
  { id: "w7-204-the-shadow-on-the-wall", title: "The shadow on the wall", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Soot saw a giant shadow at the bank and called Ember to lock the safe. The monkey clerk turned the lamp and found a small moth on its glass. Soot put his hat over the insect and carried it outside. Ember counted the coins and found none missing. Soot wrote Moth on the case file. He kept the lamp farther from the wall, and the bank opened in time to buy the morning bananas." },
  { id: "w7-180-the-morale-plant", title: "The morale plant", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Cori gave Cypress a plant to boost morale. The monkey clerk had asked for a new lamp, since his desk sat in the dark. The plant drooped there too. Cypress moved it to the bright window and took the window desk as well. Cori noticed that both looked better. He bought a lamp for the old desk and kept the plant by the sun. Cypress named it Request and watered it at lunch each day." },
  { id: "w7-209-the-witness-tail-curl", title: "The witness tail curl", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Flint thought Fern lied because her tail curled when he asked about the safe. The monkey witness said her chair was too close to the hot pipe. Flint moved it and asked again. Her tail relaxed, and she named the clerk who had changed the lock. Flint checked the receipt and found a legal repair. Fern helped him file the case. He gave her the cool chair and put a guard over the pipe." },
  { id: "w7-171-the-badge-gate-loop", title: "The badge gate loop", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Elm left his badge on his desk behind the locked gate. Pine asked the monkey worker to show it before entry. Elm pointed through the bars, where the badge lay in plain sight. Pine could see it but could not reach. Elm hooked it with his tail through the rail and held it up. Pine opened the gate. They put a spare badge locker outside and shared bananas while they fitted a simple lock." },
  { id: "w7-217-the-prairie-hat-well", title: "The prairie hat well", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Clay lost his broad hat down the well. Fenn offered a hook, but the monkey decided to go down like a hero. His tail tangled in the rope before he reached the water. Fenn pulled him up and used the hook herself. The hat came back full of water and one banana leaf. Clay let it dry on the fence. He bought Fenn bananas and kept the hook beside the well for future rescues." },
  { id: "w7-066-the-chess-cape", title: "The chess cape", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Chet wore a cape to every chess match. It made his monkey tail itch, but he thought it brought luck. Ora saw the cape brush three pawns off the board. They stopped and put the pieces back. Chet took the cape off and used it as a shade over their bananas. He lost the match by one move. Ora lent him her notes, and he studied them in the cool shade he had made." },
  { id: "w7-079-the-shield-soup-lid", title: "The shield soup lid", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Hazel blocked hail with her shiny shield. The monkey crowd stayed dry, but Cam could not find the lid for his soup pot. Hazel looked at the handle on her shield and saw his name on it. She gave it back before the soup boiled over. Cam lent her a broad tray for the next storm. Hazel served bananas from it when the sky cleared and kept it out of the dish rack." },
  { id: "w7-082-the-bread-door-wedge", title: "The bread door wedge", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Bram baked a loaf that rang like a bell when Greta knocked on it. The monkey baker said the crust proved his skill. Greta could not cut it even with a saw. Bram sliced a softer loaf and served it with bananas. They used the hard loaf to hold the door open while the kitchen cooled. Guests praised the fresh air. Bram put less heat in the oven and kept the bell loaf by the door." },
  { id: "w7-173-the-lunch-receipt-ruler", title: "The lunch receipt ruler", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Sage checked the lunch receipt with a ruler. Sol had spent one coin extra on bananas. The monkey auditor asked for a note on the extra cost. Sol showed her the large fruit and the smaller one on sale. Sage weighed both and found the larger was cheaper per bite. She cleared the receipt after an hour. Sol offered her half his lunch, and Sage said she would weigh costs before paper next time." },
  { id: "w7-208-the-midnight-parcel", title: "The midnight parcel", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Bram hired Gray to guard a parcel until twelve. The monkey sleuth kept it under his coat and watched every shadow. At twelve, Bram asked for it back and opened a box of cake candles. He had wanted them safe until his secret party. Gray lit each one and carried the cake inside. The guests cheered. Gray got a slice with bananas and a dry place to hang the coat he had kept shut all night." },
  { id: "w7-258-the-cooking-show-camera-bite", title: "The cooking show camera bite", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Ivy moved her camera close to film Herb taste the stew. The monkey chef knocked the lens with his spoon and left a red smear. Herb cleaned it with a soft cloth while the stew bubbled. Ivy filmed the pot from the side instead. The viewers saw the food clearly with no spoon in the way. Herb served bananas after filming, and Ivy put a safe space mark on the floor for the next shoot." },
  { id: "w7-277-the-sculpture-tail-crack", title: "The sculpture tail crack", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Grove made a tall stone monkey with a thin tail. Gilda saw a crack near its base before the opening. Grove wanted guests to see it as it was. Gilda roped the area off and tested the tail with a padded pole. It broke into the soft grass. Grove carved the stump smooth and set the fallen tail beside it. The show opened safely, with bananas on a low table well away from the heavy stone pieces." },
  { id: "w7-299-the-puppet-tail-string", title: "The puppet tail string", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Haze tied puppet strings to her monkey tail for a new trick. The puppet danced, then pulled her back into the curtain. Heath held the stand and helped untie her. They put the strings on a small hand frame instead. Haze could bow without moving the puppet now. The show ended with a neat dance and no torn cloth. Heath gave the puppet a wooden banana, while Haze ate the real bananas after the curtain fell." },
  { id: "w7-056-the-oven-timer-duet", title: "The oven timer duet", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Kit had ten minutes to bake buns on the show. Sam sang the last count so slowly that the monkey thought he had an hour. His buns burned while Sam held the last note. Kit sliced off the dark crust and made crunchy bits for soup. He served bananas as dessert. Sam got a real clock for the next round. Kit asked him to sing only when the food had left the oven." },
  { id: "w7-218-the-stagecoach-bench-vote", title: "The stagecoach bench vote", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Dust drove the coach so fast that Della bounced off her seat. The monkey guests voted to stop until he slowed down. Dust claimed the mail needed speed. Della showed him the letters shaken open in the rack. He tied them with a cord and set a slower pace. The coach reached town with every page intact. Della bought bananas for the guests, and Dust checked the wheels for loose bolts, then joined them." },
  { id: "w7-224-the-stolen-replica-spoon", title: "The stolen replica spoon", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Glint stole a silver spoon from the gallery. Gem found the monkey hiding it under his fur at the gate. She showed him the real spoon, locked in a glass case. His was a wooden model painted gray. Glint gave it back and asked how to carve one himself. Gem put him in the shop for a lesson after he paid the fine. He made a plain spoon and used it to eat mashed bananas at home." },
  { id: "w7-230-the-grand-vault-dust", title: "The grand vault dust", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Opal broke into the old vault and found years of dust. Orin closed the door behind the monkey and asked who would pay to clean the mess. Opal put down his bag and picked up a broom. He swept until the floor shone, then mended the latch. Orin opened the door and gave him a receipt for the repair debt now paid. Opal used his bag to carry bananas home instead of stolen gold." },
  { id: "w7-231-the-court-banana-scale", title: "The court banana scale", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Ash sued over a small banana in his lunch box. Judge Alder asked the monkey to weigh it beside the large one given to his friend. The large banana had a thick peel and less fruit. Ash weighed only the fruit and found his own share larger. He dropped the claim. Alder split both bananas between them for lunch and ordered the stall to list edible weight, so guests could compare the actual shares." },
  { id: "w7-271-the-orchestra-banana-rest", title: "The orchestra banana rest", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Ash told Alder to take a rest during the slow passage. The monkey player lay down on the stage with bananas by his tail. Ash stopped the band and told him that rest meant silence for a few beats. Alder sat back up and counted them. The tune flowed well on the next try. After the concert Ash marked a real break on the plan. Alder ate then, with his horn safe in its case." },
  { id: "w7-280-the-art-auction-cough", title: "The art auction cough", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Jun coughed at the auction and won a giant picture. The monkey guest had meant to bid on nothing. Jade paused the sale and asked for a clear raised hand. Jun drank water and kept both hands on his knees. Another guest bought the picture with a real bid. Jade placed number cards at each seat for later bids. Jun bought bananas in the lobby, where a price tag could not mistake his cough for a promise." },
  { id: "w7-031-the-wolf-choir", title: "The wolf choir", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Walt wore a wolf suit to test the door guard. Kira asked him to sing the family song before she let him in. His voice was so rough that all the young monkeys laughed. He showed his bare tail, but Kira still said no. Walt fetched his lute and learned the tune from a window. At dusk she opened the door. He brought bananas, and they gave him the low part in their choir." },
  { id: "w7-105-the-star-map-stain", title: "The star map stain", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Nix spilled tea on the star map. Pia steered toward the brown spot and found no planet. The monkey pilot checked through the window and saw that home lay just below them. Nix wiped the map clean with his tail. The stain stayed, so he marked it Tea, Not Star. They landed at the proper port and bought bananas. Pia kept the marked map to remind them where a snack break should be." },
  { id: "w7-143-the-twin-hat-clue", title: "The twin hat clue", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Flynn accused Finn of taking the red hat. Fawn wore it at the other end of the room. The monkey twins had traded seats while Flynn checked his notes. Flynn asked each to stand by a window and stay there. Finn showed a blue hat in his bag. Fawn gave the red one back to its hook. They shared bananas and labeled their bags, so Flynn could count objects and see who had moved." },
  { id: "w7-175-the-quarterly-tail-review", title: "The quarterly tail review", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Willow rated Wisp by how often his tail moved at work. The monkey clerk could file pages without moving it at all. Willow gave him low marks despite the empty inbox. Wisp tied a ribbon to a fan so it waved beside his chair. Willow praised his energy, then noticed the trick. They counted the neat stacks instead. Wisp got his fair score and a bowl of bananas, while the ribbon waved over the fan." },
  { id: "w7-206-the-gumshoe-gum", title: "The gumshoe gum", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Grit stepped in gum outside the fruit stall. Each monkey foot stuck to the next, and he could not follow the thief. Gale brought cold water and a flat scraper. Grit freed his shoes and found the fruit seller had taken the bananas inside to avoid rain. There had been no theft. He paid Gale for her work and helped sweep the stall. His new case notes began with a check of the weather." },
  { id: "w7-221-the-heist-empty-safe", title: "The heist empty safe", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Plume drew a grand plan to steal a locked safe. Puck opened it in seconds, and the monkey crew found only dust. The bananas had been moved to the pantry because a safe had no airflow. Plume paid the owner for the broken lock and asked to work off the rest. Puck fitted pantry latches instead. They earned fair wages by keeping fruit safe, and no longer hauled a steel box through the woods at night." },
  { id: "w7-253-the-reality-show-broom", title: "The reality show broom", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Chet told Gilda to fight another guest over the last broom. The monkey guest took a dust pan and swept with dry leaves instead. Chet said that made poor drama. Gilda showed him the clean floor and asked for a task worth a prize. He gave the guests a shelf to build as a team. The show aired their work with no staged row. Gilda won bananas for the neatest shelf and used the broom only later." },
  { id: "w7-050-the-wise-owl-glasses", title: "The wise owl glasses", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Odo gave advice from a high branch while wearing an owl hood. Fern asked where her lost bananas had gone. He pointed to a cloud. Fern saw them on the branch beside his tail. The monkey had worn the hood back to front and could see only through its ear holes. She turned it round and gave him the fruit. Odo checked that he could see his own feet before each new advice session." },
  { id: "w7-086-the-marathon-snack-mile", title: "The marathon snack mile", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Ria stopped at every snack stand during the long race. By the final mile the monkey carried more bananas than she could eat. Mars asked her to put the fruit down so she could finish. Ria gave each tired runner one and kept only a peel bag. She crossed last with a light tail and a full smile. Mars gave her the spare medal for best cleanup, then helped her carry the peel bag home." },
  { id: "w7-098-the-pizza-square-corners", title: "The pizza square corners", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Pru made square pizzas, but Gabe said real pizza must be round. The monkey chef cut off the corners and put them on a tray. Gabe ate his circle, then asked for the corners too. Pru charged him for a whole square. He paid and laughed. She named the corner tray after him and served bananas beside it for dessert. Gabe came back with friends who each ordered a square and kept every crisp edge." },
  { id: "w7-115-the-fake-moustache-glue", title: "The fake moustache glue", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Moss glued a false lip patch over his monkey nose. It hid his face so well that Bea would not let him into her shop. He tried to state his secret name, but the glue sealed his mouth. Bea handed him warm water through the window. Moss melted the glue and peeled the hair away. Bea trimmed his real fur and fed him bananas. Moss used a loose hat for his next guise instead." },
  { id: "w7-237-the-custody-tail-kite", title: "The custody tail kite", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Glen and Gale both claimed a kite. Grove asked each monkey to hold one end of its string. Their tails pulled apart until the paper tore. Grove stopped them and ordered a joint repair. Glen patched the paper while Gale tied a new tail. They flew it side by side at the field after court. Grove split the fee in half and ate bananas on the bench while the shared kite stayed high above them." },
  { id: "w7-203-the-alley-sax-clue", title: "The alley sax clue", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Steel heard a sad sax tune in the alley each night. He thought it marked a secret trade. The monkey watched from behind a crate of bananas until Sax opened the back door. Sax played there because his room had thin walls. Steel asked him to play inside with a rug by the door. The sound grew soft. Steel gave Sax the empty crate to sell for a mute. Both could sleep after the late night tunes." },
  { id: "w7-215-the-wanted-poster-sketch", title: "The wanted poster sketch", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Ash drew a wanted poster from a vague report. Every monkey in town had brown fur and a long tail, just like the sketch. Rowan held no one. He asked Ash to add the missing red scarf and broken boot. Only one guest wore both. The guest had lost his luggage, not stolen it, and showed the claim tag. Rowan gave back the bag of bananas and asked for written facts before the next poster." },
  { id: "w7-245-the-getaway-disguise-cart", title: "The getaway disguise cart", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Oak painted his cart to look like a bush for the getaway. Orla could not see the path through its thick leaves. The monkey driver stopped at the gate before it crashed. Oak cut a clear window and saw the bush would never fool anyone on wheels. They dropped the heist and sold the cart as a garden shade wagon. Orla took plants in it all summer, with bananas beneath the leafy roof for lunch." },
  { id: "w7-140-the-spy-magnet-spoon", title: "The spy magnet spoon", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Frost turned on a pocket magnet to catch a stolen key. Every spoon in the kitchen flew toward his monkey coat. Flora asked him to turn it off before her soup got cold. Frost caught the spoons in a bowl as they fell. The key landed among them. He opened the pantry and brought out bananas for dessert. Flora let him keep one wooden spoon, which did not move when he tested the magnet again." },
  { id: "w7-096-the-bake-sale-rival", title: "The bake sale rival", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Bina and Burt held rival bake sales across the lane. Each monkey lowered prices until a cake cost less than a crumb. Then rain drove all their guests away. Bina had a tent but no dry chairs. Burt had chairs but no tent. They joined the stalls and sold warm buns with bananas. Both earned enough to pay for flour. They kept one shared price sign and took turns holding it when the wind rose." },
  { id: "w7-195-the-vacant-office-tour", title: "The vacant office tour", pay: 244800, lib: 7, text: "Orchid showed Olive a vast office for his new fruit firm. Only one monkey worked there, peeling bananas in a corner. Olive asked how rent got paid. Orchid said future growth would cover it. Olive moved the table into a small stall outside and watched the first guests buy fruit. Orchid ended the office lease when it expired. His grand tour now took two steps, leaving more time to peel and sell the actual stock." },
  { id: "w7-236-the-exhibit-spoon", title: "The exhibit spoon", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Fenn showed a spoon as proof that a cake had been stolen. Fern asked how a spoon proved that claim. The monkey lawyer showed crumbs, but the crumbs were from his own lunch. Fern set the spoon aside and asked for the shop record. It showed the cake had been sold and paid for. Fenn cleaned the spoon and gave it back to the cook. He ate bananas with his hands while he rewrote the report." },
  { id: "w7-260-the-detective-show-clue-light", title: "The detective show clue light", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Kestrel checked a dark room for the prop clue. Kit dimmed the lamp further to make the scene tense. The monkey actor stepped on the clue and broke it. Kit turned the light up and fetched a spare prop clue. They cleared the broken bits, reset the clue, and shot again with enough light to see. Kestrel solved the case on camera. Kit saved the darkest lamp setting for the credits, after every actor left." },
  { id: "w7-296-the-mural-window-block", title: "The mural window block", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Ember painted a bright mural over the shop front, even the window. Elm could no longer see the monkey guests arrive. Ember peeled the paint off the glass and framed the window with vines instead. Guests could see bananas inside, and Elm could wave them in. The mural still looked lively along the wall. Ember signed it beside the clear pane and drew future wall plans on one sheet and window plans on another." },
  { id: "w7-169-the-lost-form-folder", title: "The lost form folder", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Flint lost the form needed to request a new form. Laurel asked for the old form as proof. The monkey guest showed his empty folder. Laurel stared at it until Flint offered her bananas from his other bag. She ate one and thought again. Laurel wrote Lost on a fresh sheet and let Flint sign it. He got the form he needed. She kept the empty folder as a place to put rules that needed review." },
  { id: "w7-232-the-witness-chair-squeak", title: "The witness chair squeak", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Bea sat in the witness chair and it creaked. Birch thought the sound meant the monkey was nervous. Bea shifted her tail, and the chair creaked again. She stood to give her account clearly. The clerk found a loose bolt beneath the seat. Birch paused the hearing while it was fixed. Bea then sat without a sound and told the same facts. The judge weighed those facts alone, with no note about the faulty chair." },
  { id: "w7-244-the-safecracker-ear-cone", title: "The safecracker ear cone", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Nix pressed a cone to the safe to hear its clicks. Nell asked the monkey why he had not tried the key she gave him. Nix said his craft needed time. The cone picked up the kitchen timer instead. Nell opened the safe with her key and took out the shop coins. Nix said he had guessed every sound. He gave the fee back and helped Nell count the coins before they bought bananas." },
  { id: "w7-147-the-portal-curtain", title: "The portal curtain", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Orbit built a portal behind his kitchen curtain. Opal stepped through to fetch bananas and landed in the tool shed. The monkey mage had linked the wrong doors. Opal came back with a rake and asked where lunch was. Orbit moved the link to the pantry, then hung a clear sign on the curtain. They ate side by side in the kitchen. The rake stayed by the back door, which led to the garden without magic." },
  { id: "w7-186-the-budget-banana-peel", title: "The budget banana peel", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Grove cut the bin budget to save coins. Gilda stacked banana peels in a corner because the monkey office had no bins left. Grove slipped on one and broke a desk leg. Gilda paid for a cheap bin from the spare coin jar and swept the floor. Grove added the desk repair to his savings chart. The total fell below zero. He renewed the bin budget and thanked Gilda for the clean walk to his chair." },
  { id: "w7-199-the-training-video-pause", title: "The training video pause", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Sable played a safety film about lifting fruit boxes. Snow saw a real box lean off the shelf behind him. The monkey clerk paused the film and caught it. Sable scolded her for missing the safety lesson, then noticed the box over his head. He helped her lower it. They used that box for the next live lesson and put the film away. Snow taught the proper grip with her tail clear of the floor." },
  { id: "w7-270-the-space-opera-wig", title: "The space opera wig", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Vale wore a vast silver wig as ruler of the stars. The monkey could not fit through the ship door. Wren took the wig off and tested the doorway with a small cap. Vale could enter, sit, and reach the buttons at last. Wren put the silver hair on the throne behind him. It looked grand in the wide shots. Vale ate bananas without hair in his mouth, and the ship scenes ended on time." },
  { id: "w7-095-the-hero-hotline-hold", title: "The hero hotline hold", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Calla rang Hugh because her kite was stuck in a tree. A taped voice told the monkey to hold. Calla put the phone down and built a stool from her fruit crates. Hugh picked up just as she freed the kite. She asked him to help put the crates back instead. He arrived with bananas and did the heavy lifting. Hugh cut the hold message and kept a pencil by the phone to note each real job." },
  { id: "w7-264-the-epic-speech-wind", title: "The epic speech wind", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Oak gave a vast speech on a hill while wind tugged his monkey cape. Orla could hear none of the words. Oak tried yelling, then lost his hat down the slope. The crew filmed his stance without sound and taped the speech indoors later. Oak fetched the hat and wrapped the bananas inside it for lunch. Orla kept the wind in the final scene, but the viewers could finally hear what the hero had said." },
  { id: "w7-268-the-film-festival-queue", title: "The film festival queue", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Sable brought a short film to the film fair. The entry speech took longer than the film, and the monkey viewers waited with tired tails. Snow cut the speech to one line and started the reel. All guests saw the full story before the hall closed. Sable thanked Snow and served bananas outside after the credits. At the next event she printed her notes on a small card, leaving the screen for the film itself." },
  { id: "w7-075-the-villain-tea-break", title: "The villain tea break", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Vee stood on a crate to declare his plan to steal all the bananas. Herb waited in peace until the monkey villain lost his voice. Herb offered tea. Vee sat down and said he wanted fruit for his hungry guests. Herb led him to the market, where the bruised fruit cost little. Vee bought enough and gave up his grand plot. Herb carried the crate home so Vee could use it as a tea table." },
  { id: "w7-078-the-tiny-ray-rescue", title: "The tiny ray rescue", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Hank shrank a jammed cart to get it through the gate. The bananas inside became so small that the monkeys needed a lens to eat them. Mayor Miri asked him to undo the ray. Hank grew the cart back outside, then took off its wheels and carried it through on its side. Miri paid him with one full banana. Hank used the ray only on the empty gate key, which fit his pocket much better." },
  { id: "w7-081-the-frozen-yogurt-race", title: "The frozen yogurt race", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Frost made yogurt so cold that the spoon froze to his fur. Jade waited for a taste while the monkey hopped around the kitchen. He held his tail near a warm lamp until the spoon fell free. Jade asked for small cups that thawed faster. Frost filled them and added bananas at the last moment. The judges ate before the next freeze. Frost won a warm pair of gloves and used them to carry the cups." },
  { id: "w7-120-the-secret-tunnel-sign", title: "The secret tunnel sign", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Alder made a hidden tunnel to his spy hut. Gus could not find it and spent an hour going round the grove. The monkey agent wanted to keep the route secret, but his lunch guest had all the bananas. Alder hung a small sign that said Roots with an arrow toward the hatch. Gus read it and knocked. After lunch they changed the sign to a plain leaf mark that both could read from the path." },
  { id: "w7-181-the-startup-bell-schedule", title: "The startup bell schedule", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Dahlia put in a bell that rang when Dax should change tasks. It rang while the monkey fixed a line of code, so he lost his place. Dax cut power to it and fixed the fault. Dahlia said the tracker showed no work done. Dax opened the working app on her screen. She tried it and rang the bell by hand in praise. They kept it for jobs done and let the clock handle lunch." },
  { id: "w7-188-the-elevator-pitch-stairs", title: "The elevator pitch stairs", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Iris tried out her lift pitch all week. Ivy worked above in a hall with no lift. The monkey founder climbed six flights and arrived too winded to give the speech. Ivy handed her water and asked what she sold. Iris said Light Bags. Ivy bought one to carry bananas down the stairs. Iris used the money to make more bags and put the speech away until she could say it in one breath." },
  { id: "w7-261-the-movie-explosion-cart", title: "The movie explosion cart", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Lark wanted Laurel to leap from a cart as smoke burst behind it. The monkey stunt actor asked where the cart would stop. Lark had planned only the leap. Laurel fitted a brake and marked a soft landing patch. They tested the route without smoke before filming. The shot looked grand and no fruit spilled from the prop crate. Laurel ate the bananas after the scene, while Lark added a stop point to every later stunt plan." },
  { id: "w7-276-the-gallery-blank-frame", title: "The gallery blank frame", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Fenn hung an empty frame and called it the essence of bananas. Fern asked the monkey artist why the real fruit sat hidden in a drawer. Fenn said the gap invited thought. Fern put one banana in the frame and let guests draw its shape on scrap paper. They stayed longer than before. Fenn served the fruit after the session and hung the art next day, with the same frame around the newest sketch." },
  { id: "w7-061-the-goalie-fruit-basket", title: "The goalie fruit basket", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Gus had no gloves for the big match. Nell gave him two fruit baskets. The monkey caught each ball, but bananas fell out at every save. The crowd ate them and cheered. At the last kick, a peel lay beside his foot. Gus used his tail to sweep it clear and caught the ball cleanly. Nell bought real gloves with the prize coins. Gus kept a basket by the goal for snacks at the break." },
  { id: "w7-084-the-secret-menu-tail", title: "The secret menu tail", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Cher kept a secret menu behind the counter. Gus guessed every code he knew, but none worked. The monkey leaned on his tail and knocked the menu onto the floor. It listed plain beans and bananas at half price. Cher said the secret was meant for regular guests. Gus came back each week, paid for lunch, and washed his own bowl. Cher put the menu on the wall so new guests could join him." },
  { id: "w7-155-the-mission-plaque-door", title: "The mission plaque door", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Basil hung a huge mission plaque over the door. Clio could not carry boxes of bananas through without tilting her monkey head. Basil said the words would inspire the team. Clio asked him to read them from the hall. He could see only the frame. They moved the plaque to a side wall and cleared the door. Clio got the boxes in before noon. Basil wrote Keep Door Clear on a smaller card by the hinge." },
  { id: "w7-187-the-email-reply-chain", title: "The email reply chain", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Heath emailed one query to the troop. Holly replied, then every monkey replied to thank her. The inbox filled while the work waited. Holly sent a last note that asked for no more thanks. It caused another dozen replies. Heath walked to each desk and asked them to stop. He wrote the answer on the wall for anyone who needed it. Holly shut her mail app and did the job before the kettle boiled." },
  { id: "w7-214-the-gold-pan-dinner", title: "The gold pan dinner", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Pip panned the creek all day and found no gold. The monkey brought the empty pan to Pru, who filled it with beans and bananas. Pip ate and noticed that the heavy pan stayed warm. He sold similar pans to the camp cooks instead of digging another hole. Pru tested each one over the stove. By winter Pip had a steady trade, and the creek ran clear where he no longer stirred the mud." },
  { id: "w7-242-the-frontier-piano-key", title: "The frontier piano key", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Lark played one tense tune each time the saloon door opened. Laurel wanted a gentler song for lunch, but his piano had only six working keys. The monkey opened the lid and found bananas stacked against the strings. Laurel had stored them there in the cool dark space. They moved the fruit to a cabinet and tuned the freed keys. Lark played a happy lunch song, and the door could open with no hint of a duel." },
  { id: "w7-250-the-heist-crew-invoice", title: "The heist crew invoice", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Sable hired Stone to build a tunnel for a heist. Stone sent a bill larger than the value of the stolen bananas. The monkey planner checked each charge and found digging, boards, and cart hire all cost real money. Sable stopped the theft and paid Stone for the work done. They turned the short tunnel into a cool fruit cellar with consent of the owner. Sable rented shelf space there and earned the money back over a season." },
  { id: "w7-286-the-poster-face-price", title: "The poster face price", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Pine made a poster with a huge monkey face and no fruit. Pax asked how guests would know he sold bananas. Pine said the face looked warm. Pax set a real bunch beside the draft and asked for its shape on the page. Pine drew it and added the price. More guests came to the stall that day. He kept the face small in the corner, where it could smile without hiding what was for sale." },
  { id: "w7-087-the-ski-lift-scarf", title: "The ski lift scarf", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Sky wore a scarf twice as long as her tail. It caught on the ski lift and pulled her monkey cap off. Liz stopped the lift before the knot grew tight. Sky cut the scarf into short pieces and wrapped each pole handle. Her hands stayed warm on the next run. Liz used the spare piece to line her lunch box. Both ate bananas at the bottom, with no loose wool near the gears." },
  { id: "w7-104-the-time-machine-cake", title: "The time machine cake", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Tess used her time machine to save a burnt cake. She went back one minute, then tripped over her own tail and missed the oven again. The monkey tried twice more and found three copies of herself in the kitchen. Ben gave each Tess a job. One watched the clock, one washed dishes, and one sliced bananas. The first Tess baked a fresh cake. They ate four slices before the machine drew them back into one." },
  { id: "w7-168-the-queue-number-zero", title: "The queue number zero", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Kestrel gave Moss ticket Zero and called One through Ten. The monkey guest sat all morning with bananas getting soft in his bag. Moss asked when Zero would come. Kestrel checked the board and found it started at One. She served him next, then printed a new first ticket. Moss shared his soft fruit with the waiting guests. Kestrel put Zero in a frame to show that a neat count must still include the first person." },
  { id: "w7-189-the-server-room-fern", title: "The server room fern", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Jade filled the server room with ferns to make it calm. Jun saw water drip onto a cable while he checked the fans. The monkey tech moved the pots outside and dried the floor. Jade asked why the room looked bare again. Jun showed her the hot air path each fern had blocked. They made a garden by the break room instead. Jade watered it there, and Jun could hear the servers humming without a drip." },
  { id: "w7-213-the-horse-tail-saddle", title: "The cowboy cart ride", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Reed arrived at the stable in full cowboy gear. Stella had no horse, only a cart pulled by two monkeys. Reed refused to ride until he saw the cart shade and the bananas in its basket. He sat down and held his hat over his tail. The ride reached town faster than his planned walk. Reed paid both pullers and helped them oil the wheels before taking the cart back along the dusty lane." },
  { id: "w7-267-the-silent-film-sneeze", title: "The silent film sneeze", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Reed played a silent hero with a solemn face. His monkey fur tickled his nose, and he sneezed during the take. Rue matched the sneeze with a sharp piano chord. The crew laughed and kept filming. Reed turned it into a scene where the hero blows dust off a lost gold map. Rue played a light tune as he found the bananas marked on it. The final film had no speech, but the sneeze still got the biggest laugh." },
  { id: "w7-179-the-onboarding-tail-maze", title: "The onboarding tail maze", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Cedar gave Nettle a stack of guides on her first day. The monkey could not see the door over the pages. She set the stack down and asked where to put her coat. Cedar found the coat hooks hidden behind a poster about welcome habits. He moved it, then led her through the office with one short map. Nettle filed the guides and took her first real task, sorting mail that had waited all morning." },
  { id: "w7-252-the-laugh-track-leak", title: "The laugh track leak", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Bea gave a sad speech while Sol played a loud laugh track. The monkey actor stopped and pointed to the wrong tape. Sol rewound it, but laughs still filled the room. Bea cut power to the speaker and spoke in silence. The crew heard the scene clearly at last. They ate bananas during the reset. Sol labeled each tape by mood, and Bea let him test the sad one before she began her next line." },
  { id: "w7-254-the-quiz-prize-box", title: "The quiz prize box", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Dara won the quiz and got a huge stone bowl. The monkey player lived in a small tree hut. Dell asked her to pose beside the prize while her tail shook as she tried to lift it. Dara asked to swap it for seeds. The show agreed. She planted bananas and sent a photo when the first fruit grew. Dell used that image in the next prize list, where each gift now had a choice of size." },
  { id: "w7-275-the-bass-note-floor", title: "The bass note floor", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Ember struck one low note and felt the stage shake. The monkey bassist stopped before the next chord. Elm checked beneath the boards and found a loose support. They moved the crowd to the yard while he fixed it. Ember played on a solid crate, with her tail clear of the strings. The outdoor show sounded good. Elm ended the repair before rain came, and the bananas served at the break stayed under the tent." },
  { id: "w7-287-the-folk-song-kettle", title: "The folk song kettle", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Quill wrote a ballad about the old kettle. The monkey claimed it had crossed seas and lasted through wars. Quartz showed him the shop receipt from last spring. Quill rewrote the song about a kettle that made good tea each day. The chorus was short enough for guests to join. Quartz served bananas during the encore. Quill sang the true price as a joke, and all guests knew what the useful little kettle had really done." },
  { id: "w7-211-the-saloon-door-swing", title: "The saloon door swing", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Sage strode through the saloon doors, which swung back and caught his monkey tail. Oak helped him free it before the piano tune ended. Sage wanted the doors fixed before the next grand entry. Oak fitted soft edges and a catch that held them open. Sage tested the walk slowly, then ordered bananas at the bar. He kept one hand on the door when he left, so the next guest could come in safely." },
  { id: "w7-269-the-superhero-trailer-chair", title: "The superhero trailer chair", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Thorn cut a trailer that made Thyme lifting a chair look like saving the world. The monkey actor asked what the full movie would show. Thorn watched the source reel and saw only a room move. He recut the trailer as a funny tale about finding space for guests. Viewers came for that story and enjoyed it. Thyme carried bananas to the first show, then put the same chair beside the table where people could really sit." },
  { id: "w7-285-the-museum-audio-nap", title: "The museum audio nap", pay: 248200, lib: 7, text: "Oak taped a long audio guide for one small bowl. Orla heard it until the monkey fell asleep on a bench. Oak found her there beside a bag of bananas. He cut the guide to a short account of who made the bowl and how it was used. Orla woke and tried the new version. She could now tour the whole room before lunch. Oak kept extra facts in a booklet for guests who chose to stay longer." },
  { id: "w7-161-the-startup-pivot-bench", title: "The startup pivot bench", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Fern planned an app to find seats. Bly built a bench for the demo. The monkey founder changed the plan to a snack app, so Bly put bananas on the bench. Fern changed again to a fitness app. Bly asked guests to walk to the bench for lunch. They paid for the food and sat down happily. Fern kept the bench service and dropped the app. Bly wrote the price on one plank in large clear letters." },
  { id: "w7-222-the-getaway-cart-brake", title: "The getaway cart brake", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Dune planned a heist of the prize melon. Drift waited in the getaway cart with his monkey tail over the brake. The melon rolled onto the cart, but the cart would not move. Dune pushed until the owner arrived. Drift lifted his tail, then chose to stay. They gave back the melon and paid for its bruise with bananas. The owner hired them to move the rest of the crop, after testing the brake first." },
  { id: "w7-163-the-funding-jar-echo", title: "The funding jar echo", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Gale brought an empty jar to Ike and called it a new fruit hub. Ike tapped it and liked the echo. The monkey founder asked for cash to make more empty jars. Ike instead put bananas inside and asked Gale to sell them. Gale sold every jar at the market that day. He brought the bills back without a fancy name. Ike funded the next crop, and Gale used the echo jar to store small coins." },
  { id: "w7-166-the-permit-for-a-chair", title: "The permit for a chair", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Rowan bought a chair but could not sit until Iris cleared it. Iris tested the legs with her monkey hands, then asked for a diagram of the tail hole. Rowan stood to draw it. Iris sat to review it and found the seat quite safe. Rowan asked if that counted as a test. Iris stamped the form and stood up. Rowan finally sat, ate bananas, and used the cleared diagram to make a cushion that fit the hole." },
  { id: "w7-097-the-relay-tail-knot", title: "The relay tail knot", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Rai and Rem tied tails to prove their team bond. The monkeys could run in a line but not turn at the track bend. They fell into the soft grass beside the bananas. Rem untied the knot and handed Rai a short stick instead. Rai ran his leg, passed the stick, and cheered from the edge. Rem crossed the line without hauling a friend. They tied a knot in the prize ribbon and hung it over the stick." },
  { id: "w7-133-the-clone-chore-chart", title: "The clone chore chart", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Suri made a clone to do her chores. Sal was another monkey who also wanted a clone to do his chores. Suri stopped the machine before it made a third. They split the list, with Suri washing dishes and Sal on broom duty. The work ended sooner than they had hoped. They ate bananas on the clean floor. Suri changed the machine label to Friend Maker and kept the switch off unless a guest truly wished to stay." },
  { id: "w7-257-the-weather-show-window", title: "The weather show window", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Gale read a report of clear skies while rain hit the studio window. Gus pointed at the script, asking the monkey to keep going. Gale set the page down and looked outside. She told viewers to bring coats, then opened the window to show the rain. Gus fetched a towel for the wet floor. They amended the report and moved the bananas away from the sill. The next script left a blank for what Gale saw herself." },
  { id: "w7-142-the-ringing-empty-box", title: "The ringing empty box", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "A box rang on the counter though no one had put a bell inside. Flint held it to his ear and shook it while Cora watched. The monkey finally opened the bottom flap. A small clock had slipped between the layers of card. Cora stopped its alarm and found the shop receipt tucked beside it. Flint packed the bananas in a new box. Cora took the clock home, where it woke her in time to open the shop." },
  { id: "w7-162-the-infinite-free-trial", title: "The infinite free trial", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Frost offered a free trial of his banana club. Uma signed up each week with a new hat and got more fruit. The monkey founder ran out of stock before anyone paid. Frost asked her to show her tail instead of her hat. Uma said it was the same tail every time. She paid for one month and helped sort the signups. Frost kept the free sample to one banana, which was still enough to taste." },
  { id: "w7-170-the-window-height-rule", title: "The window height rule", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Maple ordered the service window raised to keep tails off the counter. Oak, a short monkey clerk, could no longer see guests. He stacked boxes of bananas to reach it. Maple saw the boxes wobble and asked him to stop. Oak moved the window lower and added a rail for tails instead. Maple tested it with her own tail and signed the change. The fruit went back into storage, and Oak served guests from the floor." },
  { id: "w7-220-the-deputy-badge-shine", title: "The deputy badge shine", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Dew rubbed his badge until it flashed across the town. Silt asked the monkey to find a missing fruit cart. Dew kept at it, sure the shine would scare any thief. Silt traced the cart tracks to a loose wheel by the creek. Dew used the badge pin to hold a patch in place while Silt fixed the axle. They brought the bananas home. Dew let the badge stay scuffed, since it had finally done useful work." },
  { id: "w7-227-the-museum-wax-fruit", title: "The museum wax fruit", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Keen crawled beneath red beams to reach a display of gold bananas. Kia watched the monkey from the door. She turned the beams off and pointed to the open gift stall. The gold fruit was wax, sold for one coin each. Keen paid for one and put it in his bag. Kia let him leave after he wiped his muddy crawl marks off the floor. He kept the wax fruit on his desk, still whole." },
  { id: "w7-158-the-team-spirit-costume", title: "The team spirit costume", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Bram gave each worker a bright team cape. Wil wore his over his monkey fur, but the cape dragged through glue at the packing bench. Every box stuck to him. Bram tried to help and stuck his own cape there too. Wil cut both capes free and used the cloth as packing pads. The boxes shipped safely. Bram ordered plain aprons next time and gave each worker bananas instead of another speech about team spirit." },
  { id: "w7-248-the-noir-window-blind", title: "The noir window blind", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Quill kept the blinds shut to make his office look grave. Quartz came to ask about a missing cart, but the monkey sleuth could not read the receipt in the gloom. She opened one blind. The cart stood outside the window, where the driver had parked it. Quill gave the fee back and helped carry the bananas in. He kept the blind open for the next client, saving the dark room for naps after work." },
  { id: "w7-297-the-poetry-book-page-gap", title: "The poetry book page gap", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Fenn placed one word on each page of his poem. Fern needed a thick cover for the monkey book, though the poem lasted only a minute aloud. She laid the pages side by side on one sheet and asked him to read it. The rhythm stayed the same. Fenn chose that version and spent the saved paper on another poem. Fern bound both in a thin book, which fit beside the bananas in his small travel bag." },
  { id: "w7-100-the-hero-retirement-box", title: "The hero retirement box", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Hale packed his hero mask for his rest. Star wanted it, but the box also held bills for every broken window Hale had left behind. The young monkey read them and took a broom instead. Star swept the glass from the last rescue while Hale paid for repairs. They ate bananas on the new porch. Hale gave Star the mask at sunset, and Star put a repair fund beside it before she planned her first patrol." },
  { id: "w7-193-the-lunch-room-rebrand", title: "The lunch room rebrand", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Myrtle renamed the lunch room the Fuel Hub. Moss asked for a new stove because the old one would not heat soup. The monkey boss ordered a shiny sign instead. Moss served cold soup beneath it. Myrtle took one taste and called the repair crew. They fixed the stove that day. Moss hung a small card under the sign that said Hot Lunch At Noon. All staff used that name, since it told them when to come." },
  { id: "w7-196-the-policy-rain-test", title: "The policy rain test", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Poppy told Pebble to post all permits outside. Rain soaked them until the ink ran. The monkey clerk could no longer prove the fruit stall was legal. Poppy came back to issue a fine, but her own note got wet. Pebble lent her a clear sleeve and put one on each permit. Poppy voided the fine and added Dry Cover to the rule. The bananas stayed under the awning while every form stayed clear beside them." },
  { id: "w7-238-the-courtroom-wig-vent", title: "The courtroom wig vent", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Heath wore a huge white wig in court. The monkey judge leaned forward and blocked the desk fan. Holly saw the papers heat and curl beside his lamp. She asked him to move the wig, but he called it a symbol of the law. Holly turned the fan toward his face. The wig blew off onto the filing rack. Heath wore a small cap from then on and let the clerk keep cool while noting each case." },
  { id: "w7-247-the-courtroom-banana-peel", title: "The courtroom banana peel", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Rue brought a banana peel to prove the hallway floor was unsafe. The monkey lawyer left it by the witness chair. Reed nearly slipped and ordered it put in a sealed box. Rue said sorry and showed the photo taken before the fall. The court used that image and kept the floor clear. Reed ruled that the hall needed a bin. Rue paid for a second bin beside his own desk, where loose proof had begun to pile." },
  { id: "w7-274-the-pop-star-mirror", title: "The pop star mirror", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Dawn wanted every strand of fur in place before her concert. Dell combed the monkey for an hour while the guests waited. One curl refused to lie flat. Dell tied a small ribbon around it and opened the stage door. Dawn sang with the curl waving above her brow. Fans copied the ribbon next day. Dawn kept the combing short from then on and ate bananas with Dell in the spare time before each show." },
  { id: "w7-291-the-radio-silence-cue", title: "The radio silence cue", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Vale acted a grim silent glare in the radio studio. Wren waited, but the monkey fans heard only empty air. She asked him to speak one short line or rustle the note in his hand. Vale tore the prop note and said he would not sign. The scene became clear without a face to see. Wren saved the glare for the cast photo, then served bananas while Vale tried keeping his paper close to the mic." },
  { id: "w7-167-the-stamp-pad-drought", title: "The stamp pad drought", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Juniper could not issue fruit permits because the stamp pad was dry. Lark asked the monkey to sign each form instead. Juniper said names lacked the right shape. Lark drew a small square around each signed name. The permits went out and the bananas reached the market before noon. Juniper ordered fresh ink that day. When it came, she used the stamp only on final forms and kept her pen beside it for dry days." },
  { id: "w7-197-the-stamp-color-feud", title: "The stamp color feud", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Quill used a red stamp, but Quartz would accept only blue ones. The monkey clerks sent a fruit permit back and forth until the page turned purple. The cart waited outside with bananas going soft. Quill signed a fresh page and Quartz signed it too. The cart left. They put both stamps in a drawer and used plain names from then on. The purple page became a desk mat to show how much ink their silly feud could waste." },
  { id: "w7-241-the-train-bandit-timetable", title: "The train bandit timetable", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Kestrel waited by the track to rob the noon train. Kit walked past with bananas and asked what the monkey was doing. Kestrel pointed at the rails. Kit showed him a notice that the route had closed last year. Kestrel took his mask off and helped Kit clear weeds from the old train stop. The town opened a fruit stall there. Kestrel sold tickets for cart rides instead, keeping each time on a sign he could read." },
  { id: "w7-259-the-reunion-show-missing-chairs", title: "The reunion show missing chairs", pay: 251600, lib: 7, text: "Jade booked eight guests and six chairs for the reunion show. Jun refused to fight over a seat. The monkey fetched two crates and put soft pads on them. Jade tried to ask who hated whom, but Jun asked who could help move the set after filming. All eight raised hands. They did the work before tea and bananas arrived. Jade aired that scene, which got more praise than the old clips of their rows." },
  { id: "w7-174-the-suggestion-box-lock", title: "The suggestion box lock", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Thistle locked the idea box so no one could steal ideas. Thyme had a note but no key to the slot cover. The monkey worker slid it under the box instead. Thistle found it while dusting and read the request for an open slot. He removed the cover and posted his answer beside it. Thyme put bananas on the shelf as thanks. Thistle ate one and left the box open for the next small useful note." },
  { id: "w7-228-the-key-mold-crumble", title: "The key mold crumble", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Locke made a copy of the vault key out of dough. Lio baked it, but the teeth curled in the oven. The monkey planner tried to flatten them and broke the key in half. Lio served both bits with bananas and asked why he had not asked for a real key. Locke went to the owner and applied for work. He earned a legal key to the store room, and Lio baked plain rolls for his first shift." },
  { id: "w7-103-the-robot-tail-brush", title: "The robot tail brush", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Bo told Rex to tidy the room. Rex, a monkey in a metal suit, brushed the tail of Bo into a stiff cone and stacked bananas on it. Bo asked why the floor was still dusty. Rex said the tail had been the closest loose object. Bo moved the fruit to a bowl and showed Rex the broom. Rex swept one tile at a time. Bo sat still until the room was clean, then washed his tail back into shape." },
  { id: "w7-226-the-jewel-swap-label", title: "The jewel swap label", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Jewel packed two gems, one real and one false, for a swap at the fair. Juno put both in plain boxes. The monkey planner could not tell which held which. She asked the seller to test them and told the seller her plan before any swap. The seller kept the real gem and paid Juno for the fine model. Jewel sold bananas to cover the fine, then labeled every box in the shop before going home." },
  { id: "w7-279-the-ballet-tail-balance", title: "The ballet tail balance", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Iris tucked her tail into a belt for the ballet. The monkey tipped to one side on each turn. Ivy asked why she hid the tail, and Iris pointed to a rule in the old book. Ivy undid the belt and let her try again. Iris spun neatly with her tail held out. They changed the rule and marked the safe space around each dancer. Iris ate bananas after class, her tail resting freely over the bench." },
  { id: "w7-130-the-blue-fur-case", title: "The blue fur case", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Davy saw blue fur on Paz and asked who had hurt him. The monkey painter showed him a mural of the sea. He had leaned into the wet paint as he reached for bananas. Davy fetched soap and helped wash his tail. The blue faded, but one patch stayed on his ear. Paz kept it until the mural dried. Davy wrote the case up as Paint Spill and used the spare soap to clean his desk." },
  { id: "w7-137-the-secret-handshake-ache", title: "The secret handshake ache", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Dawn and Dell devised a secret hand grip with twelve turns and a tail twirl. The monkeys forgot the last twist and tied their tails in a knot. Dawn reached for bananas with one free hand while Dell read the rules. They undid the knot by turning the other way. Their new hello was one plain nod. Dell burned the old rules in the stove and used the warm pan to cook a snack before they left for work." },
  { id: "w7-198-the-desk-plant-promotion", title: "The desk plant promotion", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "River praised Rain for the tallest plant in the office. Rain wanted credit for her work, but the monkey boss watched only the leaves. She moved the plant to his desk and left a file summary on hers. River watered the plant all week and found it quite hard. He read the summary at last and gave Rain the lead role. She took the files to the next floor and left him clear notes about water." },
  { id: "w7-246-the-contract-tail-line", title: "The contract tail line", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Pax signed a deal to sit for a picture. The bench had no tail gap, and the monkey could not keep still. Pine read the deal and found it offered only a seat. Pax asked the painter to cut a notch or refund his fee. The painter cut it, then did the picture in an hour. Pine added Tail Space to the next deal and sat at ease, holding bananas that the painter could leave out if he wished." },
  { id: "w7-282-the-theater-ghost-rope", title: "The theater ghost rope", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Lark blamed a ghost when the curtain rose by itself. Laurel traced the rope to a snag under the stool used by the monkey actor. Each time Lark leaned back, his tail pulled the rope. Laurel freed it and moved the stool. Lark bowed to the empty wings as an apology to the ghost he had named. The curtain stayed down until the right cue. Laurel ate bananas during the break without needing to watch a haunted knot." },
  { id: "w7-183-the-jargon-glossary-jam", title: "The jargon glossary jam", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Ewan asked Ember to align the fruit task flow. The monkey clerk asked if he meant sort the bananas. Ewan said the task was part of a grander plan. Ember put ripe fruit in one bin and green fruit in another. Sales stopped wasting soft stock. Ewan praised the new bins. Ember wrote Sort Fruit beside the phrase in his word book. The next clerk read that line and got to work without needing a long meeting." },
  { id: "w7-229-the-roof-rain-cover", title: "The roof rain cover", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Moon saw a metal box on the roof and planned to steal it. May caught the monkey lifting it and showed him the vent beneath. It was a rain cover, not a safe. Moon put it back before the storm arrived. May asked him to help fit the loose screws as payment for the damage. He did, then bought bananas at the market. The roof stayed dry and he looked inside boxes before making plans from then on." },
  { id: "w7-235-the-oath-echo", title: "The oath echo", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Elm asked Ember to repeat the oath. The monkey said every word, even the request to say it again. The court clerk tried not to laugh. Elm asked one plain query about the lost fruit box. Ember said that she had placed it in the shade behind the gate. The clerk fetched the bananas and checked her account. Elm wrote a clearer oath for the next hearing, without a line that sounded like part of the pledge." },
  { id: "w7-090-the-team-photo-tail", title: "The team photo tail", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Clem held the team still for a photo before the match. Phil could not fit every monkey tail in the frame. Clem curled his tail up, and all the others copied him. Now their heads hid behind the fur. Phil asked them to sit on the bench with legs to one side. He took one quick picture. The team reached the field in time and won. Clem kept the photo beside the bowl of victory bananas." },
  { id: "w7-263-the-horror-basement-bulb", title: "The horror basement bulb", pay: 255000, lib: 7, text: "Nix went down into the cellar with a dying torch. Nell held a box of fresh bulbs beside the monkey actor. The script called for dark scenes, but Nix could not see the stairs. He fitted a new bulb before the camera rolled. The scene still felt eerie because the door creaked behind him. Nell stayed close with the spare torch. They found the prop bananas on the bottom shelf and did the shot without falling over them." },
  { id: "w7-225-the-heist-rope-job", title: "The heist rope job", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Haven tied ropes across the yard to reach a roof safe. Hazel climbed one, but the monkey found the roof held only an empty water tank. Haven had misread the plan. They took the ropes down and said sorry to the owner. She needed wash lines in the same yard. Hazel fitted them neatly and Haven washed the dirty cloths. The owner paid them bananas for the work, and the tank stayed empty until the next rain." },
  { id: "w7-262-the-romance-airport-gate", title: "The romance airport gate", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Mira ran to the airport to confess her love before Moss left. The monkey found him at the wrong gate, eating bananas. His flight had moved, and he had not read the board. Mira gave the speech while they walked to the right gate side by side. Moss thanked her and agreed to call. The film boss kept the scene because Moss reached his flight on time, with no need to halt a plane on the runway." },
  { id: "w7-164-the-beta-bug-picnic", title: "The beta bug picnic", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Glen built a lunch app that sent bananas to the wrong desk. Ula got six orders while the other monkeys got none. Glen called it a beta bug. Ula wrote desk names on six cards and handed them to the cook. Lunch reached the right seats. Glen copied that simple list into the app and tested each name once. Ula passed the spare orders along and ate her own share, and Glen stopped using beta as an answer." },
  { id: "w7-240-the-appeal-ladder", title: "The appeal ladder", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Jade asked Jun to take her case to a higher court. The monkey lawyer rented a room on the top floor and carried the files up. Jade asked where the new judges were. Jun checked the notice and learned higher meant an appeals panel across town. He gave back the room key and took the files there. Jade bought bananas for the walk. Jun kept the proper address on the front page, ahead of every grand legal phrase." },
  { id: "w7-293-the-costume-drama-zipper", title: "The costume drama zipper", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Birch wore a royal coat in the period play. The monkey could not hide the bright zipper down its back. Bea sewed a flap over it, but caught his tail in the stitch. They undid the seam and made a new tail opening. The coat looked old from the seats and came off easily in the wings. Birch thanked Bea with bananas and hung the coat on a wide hook, so the flap would not crease before the next day." },
  { id: "w7-202-the-dame-with-the-wet-shoes", title: "The dame with the wet shoes", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Pearl asked Storm to find her stolen shoes. The monkey sleuth saw wet prints from her chair to the door. Pearl had put the shoes by the stove, then lost track of them. Storm fetched them but found the heels warped by heat. He lent her flat boots for the walk home. Pearl paid him with bananas and bought new heels the next day. Storm kept a shoe rack far from his own stove after that case." },
  { id: "w7-200-the-annual-report-doorstop", title: "The annual report doorstop", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Spruce printed a thick annual report for each worker. Stone could not find the desk space to open hers. The monkey used it to hold the windy door open while fruit carts rolled in. Spruce came to demand that she read it. Stone pointed to the front page, which said Remove Blocks To Sales. He let the book stay. They read the key totals on one sheet and sold all the bananas before the door swung shut." },
  { id: "w7-243-the-western-sunset-delay", title: "The western sunset delay", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Mesa wanted to ride home at sunset for a fine outline. Moss asked the monkey to leave sooner because their bananas would bruise on the dark road. Mesa waited until the sun dipped, then could not see a rut. The cart wheel sank. Moss lit a lantern and helped push it free. They reached home late and mashed the bruised fruit for the next meal. Mesa set the next trip before dusk, with the lantern packed under his seat." },
  { id: "w7-283-the-critic-paint-shoe", title: "The critic paint shoe", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Mira called the picture dull while she stepped in wet blue paint. The monkey critic left prints across the gallery floor. Moss handed her a mop before he spoke about the review. Mira cleaned each print and noticed how the blue changed under varied lights. She wrote a more careful piece about those colors. Moss hung it near the final canvas. Mira left her shoes outside the next studio and brought bananas instead of mud on her soles." },
  { id: "w7-288-the-opera-stair-breath", title: "The opera stair breath", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Reed climbed six flights before singing his grand aria. The monkey had no breath left when Rue raised the baton. Rue asked him to arrive earlier or use the lift. Reed came early next night, warmed his voice slowly, and sang the full tune. Rue moved the heavy costume up above in advance. Reed could eat bananas after the show instead of gasping on the stairs, and the guests heard every word of the final song." },
  { id: "w7-300-the-last-encore-door", title: "The last encore door", pay: 258400, lib: 7, text: "Iris took a third encore while Ivy waited to lock the hall. The monkey crowd wanted more, but the last bus would soon leave. Iris sang one brief verse, thanked all guests, and opened the side door. Guests reached the stop in time. Ivy helped her pack the mic and cables. Iris left bananas in the crew room as thanks and put a clear final song on the next program, so claps could end without another endless encore." },
  { id: "w7-273-the-guitar-hero-string", title: "The guitar hero string", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Cedar struck a grand pose and broke his guitar string. Cora handed the monkey a spare while the crowd waited. He tried the pose again, but she pointed at the sharp edge on his guitar bridge. They filed it smooth and fitted the string. Cedar played a simple tune and did not twist the guitar behind his head. The crowd sang along. Cora got bananas in the wings, and Cedar kept the spare strings beside a small file in his case." },
  { id: "w7-249-the-western-duel-coin", title: "The western duel coin", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Rust called for a duel after Rain gave him the wrong coin. The monkey seller set both coins on the counter and showed they had the same value. Rust stared at the varied faces and finally read the rims. He put his hand away from the empty holster. Rain sold him bananas at the proper price. Rust carried a small coin chart after that, and the town settled coin rows at the counter, leaving the dusty square to lizards." },
  { id: "w7-216-the-tumbleweed-toll", title: "The tumbleweed toll", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Mesa charged a coin for each dry weed that crossed the main road. River saw the monkey town funds swell as wind blew the weeds back and forth. No one could afford to drive a cart through. River caught the weeds in a fence and sold them as dry fuel. Mesa removed the toll when she saw the clear lane. They used the dry fuel to bake bananas at the town feast and kept the road open from then on." },
  { id: "w7-165-the-office-cloud-shelf", title: "The office cloud shelf", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Hazel told Clover to put all files in the cloud. The monkey clerk carried the boxes to a high shelf where steam from the kettle rose. Paper curled in the damp air. Hazel meant an online store, but had given no login. Clover moved the boxes to a dry cabinet and asked for the account. Hazel wrote it down but kept the code safe. They sorted files side by side over bananas, then moved only the needed pages online." },
  { id: "w7-272-the-drum-solo-clock", title: "The drum solo clock", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Birch played a drum solo so long that Bea missed the last bus. The monkey singer sat by the stage with her bag of bananas. Birch finally stopped when the hall clock chimed. Bea asked him to use that chime as a limit next time. They walked home side by side and shared the fruit. At the next show his solo ended in four minutes. Bea caught her bus, and Birch could pack his drums before the hall closed." },
  { id: "w7-292-the-documentary-tripod-tail", title: "The documentary tripod tail", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Ash filmed Alder sorting bananas with a shaky camera. He said the wobble felt honest. The monkey subject asked viewers to see his hands clearly. Ash set the camera on a tripod, but one leg stood on his own tail. He moved it, tested the frame, and filmed with no shake. Viewers could tell ripe fruit from green. Ash kept one shaky shot of the market outside and used the calm view for every step of the sorting lesson." },
  { id: "w7-134-the-planet-name-vote", title: "The planet name vote", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Cove named the new planet after himself. Seren said no because she had found it first. The monkeys argued until their fuel gauge flashed. They landed and saw trees full of bananas beside a clear pond. Cove wrote Snack on the map while Seren filled the fuel tank at a pump by the pond. She liked the name. They left a small flag with the pond marked on it, then flew home with fruit and enough fuel for a calm trip." },
  { id: "w7-172-the-policy-bookshelf-tilt", title: "The policy bookshelf tilt", pay: 261800, lib: 7, text: "Rose printed each policy and stacked the binders on one shelf. Reed heard the wood crack above his monkey desk. He moved the bananas and files out of the way just before it fell. Rose wanted a rule about shelf weight. Reed asked her to remove old rules first. They kept three slim binders and sent the rest to the paper mill. Reed built a sturdy shelf and left half of it empty, where the fruit could sit safely." },
  { id: "w7-234-the-lawyer-footnote-tower", title: "The lawyer footnote tower", pay: 265200, lib: 7, text: "Dell wrote a brief with more notes below than text. Dax could not find the request from the monkey lawyer for his missing cart. Dell read the pages aloud until his voice failed. Dax drew the cart on one sheet and wrote Give It Back below. Dell added proof that Dax owned it and filed that instead. The court gave back the cart, full of bananas. Dell kept the long brief under his desk to raise the short leg." },
  { id: "w7-289-the-comic-strip-tail-panel", title: "The comic strip tail panel", pay: 265200, lib: 7, text: "Sable drew a monkey leap across three panels, but the tail was gone in the middle one. Snow asked how the hero could land without balance. Sable added a small panel where the tail curled round a branch. The scene made sense, and Snow laughed at the banana peel waiting below. Sable drew the hero as he caught that too. The strip ended with both feet on dry ground and the peel in a bin, where the next reader could see it." },
  { id: "w7-281-the-novelist-locked-ending", title: "The novelist locked ending", pay: 268600, lib: 7, text: "Kestrel wrote a mystery with no final chapter. Kit asked the monkey writer where the stolen bananas had gone. Kestrel said the reader should decide. Kit found three clues that led to the pantry and asked him to open its door on the page. Kestrel wrote the scene, and showed that the cook had stored the fruit safely. Kit took the book. Kestrel left one tiny riddle about the pantry key for the next story, which had its own ending." },
  { id: "w7-156-the-pitch-deck-banana", title: "The pitch deck banana", pay: 272000, lib: 7, text: "Finn made fifty slides for his fruit service pitch. Ivo asked what the service did. The monkey founder flipped through charts until his lamp rig failed. Finn took one banana out of his bag and peeled it for Ivo. That was the whole service. Ivo paid for lunch and asked what it cost to run. Finn wrote the costs on one sheet of paper. He sold the lamp rig and bought better fruit, leaving the slide deck in its box." },
  { id: "w7-144-the-clue-tree-fruit", title: "The clue tree fruit", pay: 272000, lib: 7, text: "Grove hung red tags on limbs to mark a trail. Greer thought the tags meant ripe bananas and picked every bunch along it. He took the tags off as he went. The monkey sleuth came back to find no markers but a full basket. Greer showed him each branch he had climbed. Grove drew the route on paper while they walked. They found the lost camp tent beside the stream and ate the fruit there, with the map tucked safely under a stone." }
);
